1
00:01:02,187 --> 00:01:05,982
WHEN LIFE GIVES YOU TANGERINES

2
00:01:06,941 --> 00:01:08,568
Can we get more squid soup?

3
00:01:08,651 --> 00:01:10,070
- Okay.
- Okay.

4
00:01:10,153 --> 00:01:12,864
Come here. Get in the net.

5
00:01:14,240 --> 00:01:15,450
Let's go.

6
00:01:15,533 --> 00:01:17,911
Are we reading this or not?

7
00:01:18,536 --> 00:01:20,705
- "There was a village…"
- Welcome.

8
00:01:20,789 --> 00:01:22,999
- Come on in.
- Welcome.

9
00:01:24,501 --> 00:01:25,794
Hi, do you have a table for two?

10
00:01:25,877 --> 00:01:27,087
- You'll need to wait.
- Yeah.

11
00:01:27,170 --> 00:01:29,422
- We'll call you back soon.
- Oh, okay, thank you. Bye.

12
00:01:31,174 --> 00:01:32,342
Please wait here.

13
00:01:36,971 --> 00:01:38,681
Guys, I told you, didn't I?

14
00:01:38,765 --> 00:01:42,560
<i>Finally, the bells</i>
<i>began ringing in the middle of the forest.</i>

15
00:01:43,394 --> 00:01:45,605
<i>Along with the sounds of the card machine.</i>

16
00:01:46,523 --> 00:01:49,442
It's all Ae-sun's fault
that I can't retire.

17
00:01:49,526 --> 00:01:51,486
<i>The uproar about "garbage dumplings"</i>

18
00:01:51,569 --> 00:01:53,196
<i>is affecting handmade</i>
<i>dumpling restaurants.</i>

19
00:01:53,279 --> 00:01:54,489
It's so good.

20
00:01:54,572 --> 00:01:55,698
It's so delicious.

21
00:01:55,782 --> 00:01:58,827
<i>…because of bird flu. The same phenomenon</i>
<i>is happening to many dumpling…</i>

22
00:01:58,910 --> 00:02:00,662
Oh, let me wrap this for you.

23
00:02:00,745 --> 00:02:03,581
I'll make you an amazing seaweed wrap.
Here. Here.

24
00:02:03,665 --> 00:02:05,250
{\an8}Ah. Oh.

25
00:02:05,333 --> 00:02:07,877
Stop glaring at the customers
who ask for more soup.

26
00:02:07,961 --> 00:02:10,338
Okay, let's eat this. That and that.

27
00:02:10,421 --> 00:02:12,590
- Ae-sun, your daughter-in-law…
- Ah.

28
00:02:12,674 --> 00:02:14,134
I don't want it, Grandpa.

29
00:02:14,217 --> 00:02:15,635
Please eat it for me.

30
00:02:16,261 --> 00:02:17,720
Who will you give it to, Yeong-won?

31
00:02:18,304 --> 00:02:20,682
Your maternal grandpa
or your paternal grandpa?

32
00:02:21,182 --> 00:02:22,892
Ah. Ah.

33
00:02:23,935 --> 00:02:26,229
Ah. No. Oh!

34
00:02:27,772 --> 00:02:30,108
You can't open your mouth and then ask.

35
00:02:30,191 --> 00:02:31,860
Can we get some more squid soup?

36
00:02:31,943 --> 00:02:34,529
- Oh, okay.
- Can we have more soup here?

37
00:02:34,612 --> 00:02:36,364
- Could we also get another?
- Yes.

38
00:02:36,447 --> 00:02:40,285
Why are you putting in so much squid?
That's why they eat up everything.

39
00:02:40,952 --> 00:02:44,914
Squid soup needs to be on the menu,
or else you're going to start losing cash.

40
00:02:47,876 --> 00:02:50,628
We need to hire people.
This is too much for you.

41
00:02:51,629 --> 00:02:53,256
Who said it was too much for me?

42
00:02:54,799 --> 00:02:57,677
<i>All that money</i>
<i>made my mom dance.</i>

43
00:02:58,178 --> 00:03:00,555
<i>♪ Singing in the rain ♪</i>

44
00:03:01,181 --> 00:03:02,015
<i>♪ Singing… ♪</i>

45
00:03:02,098 --> 00:03:04,225
Why are you going down
the steps like that?

46
00:03:04,309 --> 00:03:06,269
Is menopause over?

47
00:03:08,104 --> 00:03:09,397
No, it's strange.

48
00:03:09,480 --> 00:03:11,608
I'm just in a good mood.

49
00:03:11,691 --> 00:03:15,778
We are making money, Gwan-sik. We're so
busy from early morning to late at night.

50
00:03:16,321 --> 00:03:20,533
But it's not really too tiring
'cause our bank account's growing.

51
00:03:22,202 --> 00:03:25,371
- You thrilled?
- Yes, I'm so, so thrilled.

52
00:03:25,455 --> 00:03:26,956
Maybe the heavens

53
00:03:27,040 --> 00:03:29,626
have been so stingy all these years

54
00:03:29,709 --> 00:03:31,419
to bless us all at once.

55
00:03:32,420 --> 00:03:34,380
We made a ton of deliveries
during the World Cup.

56
00:03:34,464 --> 00:03:35,924
Jeju has duty-free shops now.

57
00:03:36,007 --> 00:03:38,092
<i>All In </i>was shot in Jeju.

58
00:03:39,636 --> 00:03:42,305
Joonggonara assisted
in getting us Cheol-yong.

59
00:03:42,388 --> 00:03:45,350
Jeong Mi-in did an ad for us.
How is this our life?

60
00:03:47,143 --> 00:03:50,480
Oh, I feel maybe
we're getting paid a reward now.

61
00:03:51,522 --> 00:03:54,776
Honey,
I think we should go on vacations.

62
00:03:54,859 --> 00:03:57,195
Let's go to Guam and China.

63
00:03:57,278 --> 00:03:59,948
If a brat like Mi-suk can go,
then why can't I?

64
00:04:02,283 --> 00:04:04,911
Why do you always talk
so spitefully of her?

65
00:04:07,789 --> 00:04:10,416
Oh, if life can continue to be this,

66
00:04:10,500 --> 00:04:13,044
I think I might live
ten thousand years longer.

67
00:04:16,673 --> 00:04:19,217
<i>♪ Singing in the rain ♪</i>

68
00:04:19,926 --> 00:04:22,971
<i>♪ Just singing in the rain… ♪</i>

69
00:04:23,054 --> 00:04:27,100
<i>My parents, who once</i>
<i>so diligently dug up a field of stones,</i>

70
00:04:27,934 --> 00:04:30,478
<i>were now people</i>
<i>who had created a landmark.</i>

71
00:04:30,561 --> 00:04:32,981
<i>♪ I'm laughing at clouds ♪</i>

72
00:04:33,064 --> 00:04:36,609
♪ <i>So dark up above ♪</i>

73
00:04:37,193 --> 00:04:39,612
<i>♪ The sun's in my heart ♪</i>

74
00:04:39,696 --> 00:04:43,116
<i>♪ And I'm ready for love ♪</i>

75
00:04:43,199 --> 00:04:46,327
<i>♪ Let the stormy clouds chase ♪</i>

76
00:04:47,287 --> 00:04:49,247
Oh my, my. Mi-suk, that brat!

77
00:04:49,330 --> 00:04:51,958
How dare she call her place
"The Original"!

78
00:04:53,209 --> 00:04:55,169
Do you think you own
all the squids in Jeju?

79
00:04:55,253 --> 00:04:56,671
Did you get a trademark on it?

80
00:04:57,255 --> 00:04:59,132
What?
Did you apply for a trademark

81
00:04:59,215 --> 00:05:02,010
piggybacking on
someone else's success? Did you?

82
00:05:02,719 --> 00:05:05,555
Hang on.
You come here for another foot massage?

83
00:05:06,347 --> 00:05:08,099
I already said,

84
00:05:08,182 --> 00:05:10,101
yeah, my foot here was asleep.

85
00:05:10,184 --> 00:05:11,102
Why do you care?

86
00:05:11,185 --> 00:05:12,520
You'd better change your sign.

87
00:05:12,603 --> 00:05:13,980
Change your menu!

88
00:05:15,523 --> 00:05:17,900
Leave her alone. I'm grateful for this.

89
00:05:19,152 --> 00:05:21,237
It's better if we compete
for the same thing.

90
00:05:25,908 --> 00:05:27,744
Yeah? Why?

91
00:05:28,244 --> 00:05:32,332
Because with you there pushing fakes,
the real thing sells better.

92
00:05:35,543 --> 00:05:37,628
Uh…

93
00:05:37,712 --> 00:05:39,964
Excuse me, can we get
some more squid soup?

94
00:05:40,048 --> 00:05:40,923
Oh, okay, okay.

95
00:05:41,883 --> 00:05:43,843
Please sign here.

96
00:05:43,926 --> 00:05:45,970
DDUKBAEGI SQUID SOUP
4,000 WON

97
00:05:46,054 --> 00:05:49,640
<i>But there was someone</i>
<i>who always had a hold over her heart.</i>

98
00:05:49,724 --> 00:05:51,267
Hey, dear.

99
00:05:51,351 --> 00:05:55,730
I told you I'd eat it.
I wanted to. I wanted to.

100
00:05:55,813 --> 00:05:58,399
I wanted to. I wanted to. I wanted to.

101
00:05:58,483 --> 00:06:01,069
<i>Yes.</i>
<i>I also had someone like that.</i>

102
00:06:01,152 --> 00:06:02,570
- Momma.
- I wanted to do it.

103
00:06:02,653 --> 00:06:03,613
Me, me, me, me.

104
00:06:03,696 --> 00:06:05,656
<i>Even in my terrible 37s…</i>

105
00:06:05,740 --> 00:06:08,326
- I wanted to do it!
<i>- …I needed my mom.</i>

106
00:06:08,910 --> 00:06:11,704
I wanted to.

107
00:06:11,788 --> 00:06:14,874
- I wanted to. I wanted to.
- Aw. Okay, okay. There, there.

108
00:06:14,957 --> 00:06:17,335
Come on. I get that she's
in her terrible fours now,

109
00:06:17,418 --> 00:06:20,046
but how can she be mad
that I fed her, you know?

110
00:06:20,129 --> 00:06:23,049
She wanted to eat on her own,
and she's mad that I spoon-fed her.

111
00:06:27,762 --> 00:06:29,055
Say "bye-bye" to Mom.

112
00:06:29,138 --> 00:06:31,432
Goodbye! Goodbye!

113
00:06:31,516 --> 00:06:33,184
<i>I could only see my daughter,</i>

114
00:06:33,267 --> 00:06:34,727
<i>and my mom could only see me.</i>

115
00:06:34,811 --> 00:06:36,562
She lost weight. Even more now.

116
00:06:36,646 --> 00:06:38,356
I'll be back.

117
00:06:39,190 --> 00:06:40,525
Oh, that girl.

118
00:06:40,608 --> 00:06:41,692
She's so shy.

119
00:06:41,776 --> 00:06:43,903
<i>I recognized</i>
<i>a thousand expressions</i>

120
00:06:43,986 --> 00:06:45,154
<i>on my daughter's face,</i>

121
00:06:45,238 --> 00:06:47,698
<i>but I couldn't remember</i>
<i>any of my mother's.</i>

122
00:06:49,409 --> 00:06:51,077
<i>I didn't know it then.</i>

123
00:06:51,702 --> 00:06:54,956
<i>I didn't realize</i>
<i>the only facial expressions I'd remember</i>

124
00:06:55,456 --> 00:06:58,960
<i>were the awkward ones</i>
<i>that she made in photographs.</i>

125
00:07:05,466 --> 00:07:07,635
Oh, you stubborn child.

126
00:07:08,511 --> 00:07:10,972
Why don't you listen to your mom?

127
00:07:12,974 --> 00:07:15,184
You may be my grandchild, but

128
00:07:15,935 --> 00:07:17,812
but I don't like that you…

129
00:07:18,479 --> 00:07:19,856
you made my…

130
00:07:20,648 --> 00:07:22,108
my daughter suffer.

131
00:07:22,191 --> 00:07:24,694
You may be mean to your mother,

132
00:07:26,571 --> 00:07:28,239
but she's the…

133
00:07:30,283 --> 00:07:32,535
the most important person to me.

134
00:07:38,541 --> 00:07:40,585
Be good to my daughter.

135
00:07:42,295 --> 00:07:43,546
Be good to her

136
00:07:44,505 --> 00:07:46,466
forever and ever.

137
00:07:47,049 --> 00:07:47,967
Okay?

138
00:07:50,928 --> 00:07:56,267
<i>♪ Sleep, sleep, sweet child, sleep ♪</i>

139
00:07:57,059 --> 00:08:00,646
<i>♪ My baby is fast asleep ♪</i>

140
00:08:00,730 --> 00:08:04,484
<i>For some reason,</i>
<i>it felt so awkward to simply say,</i>

141
00:08:04,567 --> 00:08:05,693
<i>"Thank you."</i>

142
00:08:05,776 --> 00:08:07,820
Wait, who asked you
to clean the whole place?

143
00:08:07,904 --> 00:08:09,530
And why'd you clean the toilet?

144
00:08:10,114 --> 00:08:11,824
Go rest. You said you're off today.

145
00:08:11,908 --> 00:08:15,328
God, Mom, this is why
I don't want to call you over.

146
00:08:15,411 --> 00:08:19,790
Hey, Miss Terrible Thirty-sevens.
If you're thankful, just say thank you.

147
00:08:19,874 --> 00:08:22,585
I can tell you feel bad
by your… your long face.

148
00:08:24,378 --> 00:08:26,172
- Then set Sae-bom down.
- Hey.

149
00:08:26,255 --> 00:08:29,091
You've been getting cupping
for your back, you said.

150
00:08:32,428 --> 00:08:34,514
Park Sae-bom
is the first person

151
00:08:35,097 --> 00:08:38,768
who's ever made me feel
like I'm completely out of control.

152
00:08:39,769 --> 00:08:41,270
Why is she so stubborn?

153
00:08:41,938 --> 00:08:43,856
She never says yes the first time.

154
00:08:45,191 --> 00:08:47,151
Oh, sweet justice.

155
00:08:47,235 --> 00:08:49,820
Your daughter's just like you.

156
00:08:51,822 --> 00:08:52,698
Be honest.

157
00:08:53,282 --> 00:08:54,492
I frustrated you, right?

158
00:08:55,451 --> 00:08:57,578
How did you raise three kids?

159
00:08:57,662 --> 00:09:00,581
Eat the drumstick.
You do what you have to do.

160
00:09:00,665 --> 00:09:01,999
You have to live your own life

161
00:09:02,083 --> 00:09:05,086
so you don't feel resentful
about anything.

162
00:09:05,169 --> 00:09:07,296
Otherwise,
you'll always question your choices

163
00:09:07,380 --> 00:09:08,798
and wonder what could've been.

164
00:09:08,881 --> 00:09:10,258
She will figure that out.

165
00:09:10,341 --> 00:09:13,052
She'll be able to tell
just by looking at you.

166
00:09:13,803 --> 00:09:17,223
Right now,
you're Sae-bom's entire world, you see.

167
00:09:21,227 --> 00:09:22,061
But

168
00:09:23,729 --> 00:09:25,398
that won't last too long.

169
00:09:26,566 --> 00:09:28,568
You won't be a priority.

170
00:09:29,485 --> 00:09:33,197
Later in life,
she won't put you first anyway.

171
00:09:34,865 --> 00:09:36,576
So just do what you want now.

172
00:09:37,118 --> 00:09:37,952
Okay?

173
00:09:40,955 --> 00:09:42,957
Mom, do you regret anything?

174
00:09:44,125 --> 00:09:46,043
Not doing everything you wanted?

175
00:09:46,127 --> 00:09:48,838
No, I wanted to do it all.

176
00:09:50,673 --> 00:09:52,466
Oh Ae-sun, the orphan alone in the world.

177
00:09:52,550 --> 00:09:55,094
Oh Ae-sun the housekeeper.

178
00:09:55,177 --> 00:09:57,388
Dropping out of high school Oh Ae-sun.

179
00:09:58,180 --> 00:10:02,101
The best job I ever had was being
Geum-myeong and Eun-myeong's mother.

180
00:10:02,184 --> 00:10:03,561
I really lived.

181
00:10:04,854 --> 00:10:07,398
I lived life to the fullest in my own way.

182
00:10:07,481 --> 00:10:09,775
Don't look down too much on my life.

183
00:10:12,820 --> 00:10:14,030
Yeah, um,

184
00:10:14,822 --> 00:10:16,824
maybe I'm missing maternal instincts.

185
00:10:16,907 --> 00:10:18,909
Sometimes, I get so angry.

186
00:10:21,120 --> 00:10:22,830
I scream at that girl.

187
00:10:22,913 --> 00:10:24,498
I think I'm losing it.

188
00:10:24,999 --> 00:10:27,877
In the beginning,
no mother knows anything.

189
00:10:27,960 --> 00:10:30,671
Your child will grow,
and then so will you.

190
00:10:33,007 --> 00:10:34,008
Sae-bom,

191
00:10:34,091 --> 00:10:37,011
are you going to chew your food
a hundred times in the morning?

192
00:10:37,094 --> 00:10:39,472
Will you change your clothes ten times?

193
00:10:39,555 --> 00:10:42,725
Why do you give me such
a hard time every morning? Huh?

194
00:10:43,601 --> 00:10:44,435
Why?

195
00:10:45,936 --> 00:10:49,815
{\an8}If I have an early breakfast,
you leave earlier.

196
00:10:50,524 --> 00:10:53,819
If I eat and finish getting dressed,

197
00:10:54,403 --> 00:10:56,113
you go to work.

198
00:10:57,907 --> 00:10:59,492
Is that why you do that?

199
00:11:00,284 --> 00:11:01,661
So I can't go?

200
00:11:02,495 --> 00:11:03,412
Oh.

201
00:11:04,705 --> 00:11:06,123
I'm sorry

202
00:11:06,207 --> 00:11:09,210
that I yelled at you the other day, okay?

203
00:11:09,752 --> 00:11:10,795
That was my bad.

204
00:11:10,878 --> 00:11:12,755
Come here.

205
00:11:14,131 --> 00:11:15,424
Oh, you.

206
00:11:16,384 --> 00:11:18,552
Sae-bom, Mommy loves you.

207
00:11:19,220 --> 00:11:22,598
I love you so much, okay? Kisses. Hmm?

208
00:11:22,682 --> 00:11:25,768
<i>A mother's daughter</i>
<i>was now a mother herself.</i>

209
00:11:27,269 --> 00:11:30,231
<i>Mom hoped her daughter's life</i>
<i>with her own little girl</i>

210
00:11:30,314 --> 00:11:31,857
<i>wouldn't be a difficult one.</i>

211
00:11:33,025 --> 00:11:35,444
GEUM-MYEONG: GINGER TEA
SAE-BOM: CHOPPED VEGGIES

212
00:11:35,528 --> 00:11:36,737
CHUNG-SEOP: BLACK GARLIC

213
00:11:36,821 --> 00:11:38,114
<i>My whole life,</i>

214
00:11:38,197 --> 00:11:41,784
<i>my mom never failed to make time for me.</i>

215
00:11:47,957 --> 00:11:50,167
- Honey.
- Hmm?

216
00:11:50,251 --> 00:11:53,045
You know the money we saved
to buy Sae-bom a piano?

217
00:11:54,046 --> 00:11:56,382
Can we use that for my parents,
do you think?

218
00:11:58,509 --> 00:12:00,177
I think if I don't do

219
00:12:00,678 --> 00:12:03,431
anything for them, I will regret it later.

220
00:12:05,307 --> 00:12:06,142
Geum-myeong.

221
00:12:06,767 --> 00:12:07,601
Hmm?

222
00:12:07,685 --> 00:12:08,978
Stop, okay?

223
00:12:09,562 --> 00:12:12,773
You don't need to ask.
I'll leave it up to you to make the call.

224
00:12:17,528 --> 00:12:20,072
So, should I take my socks off again?

225
00:12:30,124 --> 00:12:31,459
So how much is it?

226
00:12:33,169 --> 00:12:35,629
Isn't a Seoul hospital checkup pricier?

227
00:12:36,130 --> 00:12:39,258
You guys would only do this
if I paid for it myself.

228
00:12:40,509 --> 00:12:42,511
Parents still need
to be good to their kids.

229
00:12:43,012 --> 00:12:44,680
Stay healthy for me, okay?

230
00:12:44,764 --> 00:12:46,098
Just a blood test for me.

231
00:12:47,057 --> 00:12:49,643
Come on, Dad,
both knees are totally worn out.

232
00:12:50,144 --> 00:12:52,146
And, Mom, cupping isn't a cure-all.

233
00:12:52,229 --> 00:12:54,190
So what does it come to for both of us?

234
00:12:54,273 --> 00:12:55,775
Just a blood test, all right?

235
00:12:59,069 --> 00:13:00,029
Mm.

236
00:13:03,699 --> 00:13:04,909
Hey, Yong-geon.

237
00:13:05,576 --> 00:13:06,535
I'm in Seoul.

238
00:13:07,787 --> 00:13:09,079
No, I can't come today.

239
00:13:11,999 --> 00:13:13,417
Since we have money now…

240
00:13:13,501 --> 00:13:16,337
- Oh, oh, right.
- …he's taking some guitar lessons.

241
00:13:16,420 --> 00:13:17,797
- Acoustic guitar.
- Yeah, yeah, yeah.

242
00:13:18,297 --> 00:13:19,131
Dad?

243
00:13:19,215 --> 00:13:20,341
- Ah.
- Guitar?

244
00:13:20,841 --> 00:13:22,927
Yeah, yeah, yeah.
Count me out for this lesson.

245
00:13:23,010 --> 00:13:25,471
See, when others got to play it
when they were young,

246
00:13:25,554 --> 00:13:27,973
your father never got to do
anything like that.

247
00:13:28,557 --> 00:13:30,518
Kim Kwang-seok is his amazing new hero.

248
00:13:30,601 --> 00:13:33,479
- Ah, come on.
- He has a hobby.

249
00:13:34,271 --> 00:13:35,523
First time in his life.

250
00:13:36,023 --> 00:13:38,025
PRECAUTIONS FOR ENDOSCOPY

251
00:13:45,449 --> 00:13:47,743
I told you
we should remove your moles.

252
00:13:47,827 --> 00:13:48,661
You look so…

253
00:13:49,453 --> 00:13:50,955
so tired.

254
00:13:52,998 --> 00:13:54,875
No, what I mean…

255
00:13:57,795 --> 00:13:59,463
I don't wanna go.

256
00:14:02,800 --> 00:14:03,634
What?

257
00:14:04,844 --> 00:14:06,762
Who's telling you to go anywhere?

258
00:14:08,222 --> 00:14:09,765
The thing is…

259
00:14:13,185 --> 00:14:15,688
I can't go build the barrier with you.

260
00:14:18,566 --> 00:14:22,653
I can't go and build the barrier with you.

261
00:14:29,451 --> 00:14:30,286
Dong-myeong.

262
00:14:33,038 --> 00:14:33,998
He can't.

263
00:14:36,667 --> 00:14:37,793
Dong-myeong.

264
00:14:40,754 --> 00:14:41,672
Dong-myeong.

265
00:14:44,341 --> 00:14:45,301
Dong-myeong.

266
00:14:47,928 --> 00:14:49,221
I'm on my way.

267
00:14:51,390 --> 00:14:52,308
Dong-myeong.

268
00:14:53,893 --> 00:14:54,810
Dong-myeong.

269
00:14:55,311 --> 00:14:57,021
<i>Dad kept calling out his name.</i>

270
00:14:57,104 --> 00:14:58,480
Dong-myeong.

271
00:15:00,274 --> 00:15:04,653
<i>The name that he hadn't</i>
<i>been able to say for so long.</i>

272
00:15:05,237 --> 00:15:07,114
Dong. Dong.

273
00:15:07,197 --> 00:15:08,282
Dong-myeong.

274
00:15:14,079 --> 00:15:15,456
Dong-myeong.

275
00:15:15,539 --> 00:15:17,458
<i>Mom finally got to see</i>

276
00:15:18,500 --> 00:15:21,337
<i>Dad's inner prison for the first time.</i>

277
00:15:26,008 --> 00:15:26,926
<i>Barrier?</i>

278
00:15:27,009 --> 00:15:28,427
ENDOSCOPY CENTER

279
00:15:28,510 --> 00:15:29,678
Yes, he said,

280
00:15:30,220 --> 00:15:31,680
"I shouldn't have gone

281
00:15:33,349 --> 00:15:35,017
to set up the barrier."

282
00:15:37,186 --> 00:15:38,687
"Shouldn't have gone."

283
00:15:39,855 --> 00:15:43,817
He kept saying,
"Dong-myeong, Dong-myeong."

284
00:15:44,610 --> 00:15:45,903
Now I get

285
00:15:47,154 --> 00:15:49,156
why we never talked

286
00:15:49,657 --> 00:15:51,367
about our lost son.

287
00:15:55,454 --> 00:15:57,998
Well, I asked him to tell me
when I was going under,

288
00:15:58,082 --> 00:16:01,001
but before I knew it,
they said I was done.

289
00:16:02,795 --> 00:16:04,713
Dad, would you like to eat something?

290
00:16:04,797 --> 00:16:05,923
I'll get you anything.

291
00:16:06,423 --> 00:16:08,300
- Pork belly?
- Pork belly?

292
00:16:08,384 --> 00:16:09,927
Yeah.

293
00:16:10,010 --> 00:16:11,637
<i>In their hearts</i>…

294
00:16:14,890 --> 00:16:16,433
<i>was a very small</i>

295
00:16:18,102 --> 00:16:19,728
<i>yet massive tomb.</i>

296
00:16:46,672 --> 00:16:47,965
You're silly.

297
00:16:48,882 --> 00:16:51,218
Have you been doing that alone
this whole time?

298
00:16:55,889 --> 00:16:58,517
You came today because you thought
I'd come tomorrow, huh?

299
00:16:59,018 --> 00:17:00,477
On his actual birthday.

300
00:17:01,520 --> 00:17:04,440
I followed you because
I knew you were coming here today.

301
00:17:06,567 --> 00:17:10,279
I'm sure Dong-myeong wants to see
his parents on his birthday.

302
00:17:12,740 --> 00:17:14,116
Yes, but it's different.

303
00:17:16,076 --> 00:17:20,330
Families all gather together
at the graves of their parents

304
00:17:21,457 --> 00:17:22,958
but not of their children.

305
00:17:27,254 --> 00:17:30,299
I couldn't bear… to see your face.

306
00:17:44,104 --> 00:17:46,899
We can't leave our baby alone.

307
00:17:54,406 --> 00:17:55,449
Oh no.

308
00:17:58,327 --> 00:18:00,537
I'm sure he's scared.

309
00:18:02,915 --> 00:18:04,750
He must be so scared.

310
00:18:08,545 --> 00:18:10,756
<i>Their footsteps</i>
<i>created a path,</i>

311
00:18:11,840 --> 00:18:13,550
<i>and in all four seasons,</i>

312
00:18:14,093 --> 00:18:17,513
<i>the grave where their child lay</i>
<i>was the neatest of all.</i>

313
00:18:44,748 --> 00:18:48,502
<i>Dong-myeong's grave</i>
<i>had the most adorable things</i>

314
00:18:49,461 --> 00:18:51,630
<i>that brought them the most pain.</i>

315
00:19:09,648 --> 00:19:10,691
Let's go.

316
00:19:15,988 --> 00:19:17,739
Come back to the house.

317
00:19:18,907 --> 00:19:19,741
Let's go.

318
00:19:27,249 --> 00:19:31,587
<i>I finally figured out</i>
<i>why we could never talk</i>

319
00:19:32,546 --> 00:19:33,839
<i>about Dong-myeong.</i>

320
00:19:41,263 --> 00:19:44,057
There's no reminiscing
if the guilt is bigger

321
00:19:44,683 --> 00:19:46,268
than your longing feeling.

322
00:19:49,354 --> 00:19:52,441
<i>We adored him because he was the youngest.</i>

323
00:19:53,984 --> 00:19:55,444
<i>He was an angel.</i>

324
00:20:00,657 --> 00:20:04,036
<i>At least we got to hold that angel</i>
<i>for four years.</i>

325
00:20:05,621 --> 00:20:09,041
<i>If I had the choice</i>
<i>to go through it all over again,</i>

326
00:20:10,125 --> 00:20:12,461
<i>I would so that I could hold him.</i>

327
00:20:13,378 --> 00:20:15,464
We'll see him in the next lifetime.

328
00:20:16,131 --> 00:20:17,424
That's getting closer.

329
00:20:23,013 --> 00:20:24,097
I don't want to.

330
00:20:24,598 --> 00:20:27,476
I don't want Dong-myeong
to see me after I die.

331
00:20:28,435 --> 00:20:29,311
Each day,

332
00:20:30,687 --> 00:20:33,482
I pray that my Dong-myeong
would forget about us.

333
00:20:34,608 --> 00:20:36,151
I miss him so much.

334
00:20:36,735 --> 00:20:37,736
Thinking of him

335
00:20:39,279 --> 00:20:40,906
coming to look for us…

336
00:20:43,450 --> 00:20:44,576
It hurts my heart

337
00:20:45,911 --> 00:20:47,746
thinking about how he misses us.

338
00:21:02,886 --> 00:21:04,805
When are you gonna show me?

339
00:21:09,268 --> 00:21:10,936
What's the title of today's poem?

340
00:21:16,650 --> 00:21:18,902
"The Most Adorable Uncle."

341
00:21:19,486 --> 00:21:20,570
Uncle Dong-myeong.

342
00:21:21,571 --> 00:21:24,992
When our kids told their kids,
"This is Uncle Dong-myeong,"

343
00:21:25,826 --> 00:21:27,536
it was so strange to hear.

344
00:21:28,120 --> 00:21:29,955
And as strange as it was,

345
00:21:31,790 --> 00:21:33,000
I loved it.

346
00:21:33,500 --> 00:21:36,336
Maybe Dong-myeong would feel less lonely.

347
00:21:36,878 --> 00:21:38,046
Oddly enough,

348
00:21:38,755 --> 00:21:39,673
I, uh,

349
00:21:40,173 --> 00:21:42,259
get the feeling I'm less of a bad mother.

350
00:21:45,137 --> 00:21:49,016
Listen, how could you be
a bad mother in any case?

351
00:21:49,099 --> 00:21:52,394
A dog sires a dog. A cow sires a cow.

352
00:21:52,477 --> 00:21:54,354
- Hello?
- Who would sire an angel?

353
00:21:54,438 --> 00:21:56,523
- Hey, yeah.
- Dong-myeong was our angel.

354
00:21:56,606 --> 00:21:57,649
Okay, hang on.

355
00:21:57,733 --> 00:21:59,151
Every night, I stare at your back

356
00:21:59,234 --> 00:22:01,361
while you're sleeping quietly
and dreaming.

357
00:22:01,862 --> 00:22:06,783
I can't sleep because
I find myself staring at your wings.

358
00:22:09,119 --> 00:22:12,581
Hey, Dad, the star of the family
wants to talk to you.

359
00:22:13,123 --> 00:22:15,459
Not Mom? Me? It's me she wants?

360
00:22:15,542 --> 00:22:17,586
Wake up the kids. Let's go home.

361
00:22:23,050 --> 00:22:23,925
Hey, Geum-myeong.

362
00:22:24,760 --> 00:22:26,803
What, will she be in the papers again?

363
00:22:26,887 --> 00:22:28,305
Mom? She's right here.

364
00:22:29,139 --> 00:22:30,724
I thought you wanted to talk to me.

365
00:22:31,975 --> 00:22:34,478
- Yeah.
- She wants to talk to me, right?

366
00:22:37,147 --> 00:22:37,981
Uh-huh.

367
00:22:43,236 --> 00:22:45,655
- What is it?
- Yeah.

368
00:22:46,448 --> 00:22:50,952
<i>Just as things start</i>
<i>to look up, life throws another curveball.</i>

369
00:22:51,703 --> 00:22:53,163
Really?

370
00:22:54,081 --> 00:22:55,415
What is it?

371
00:22:55,499 --> 00:22:58,377
<i>As if someone</i>
<i>was collecting an unknown debt,</i>

372
00:22:58,877 --> 00:23:01,088
<i>there was a voice from the heavens saying,</i>

373
00:23:01,713 --> 00:23:03,006
<i>"I'm sorry."</i>

374
00:23:03,715 --> 00:23:04,716
<i>"I'm sorry."</i>

375
00:23:05,384 --> 00:23:06,843
They just wanna take a second look.

376
00:23:07,844 --> 00:23:09,471
I'm sure it's nothing.

377
00:23:09,554 --> 00:23:12,724
Even if it is something, they can treat
most things now. It'll be fine.

378
00:23:12,808 --> 00:23:14,434
Mr. Yang Gwan-sik.

379
00:23:14,518 --> 00:23:16,645
- Yes, yes.
- Please wait at blood testing.

380
00:23:18,438 --> 00:23:19,981
What is going on here?

381
00:23:21,149 --> 00:23:22,901
Why is the Steelheart suffering?

382
00:23:24,611 --> 00:23:25,946
Dad.

383
00:23:27,114 --> 00:23:28,532
Don't be afraid.

384
00:23:29,199 --> 00:23:30,158
I've got your back.

385
00:23:30,242 --> 00:23:32,452
I'll be right here with you, okay?

386
00:23:34,329 --> 00:23:36,706
I'm not. I don't feel worried.

387
00:23:37,541 --> 00:23:38,750
I know my own body.

388
00:23:41,670 --> 00:23:43,463
<i>But no one knew</i>

389
00:23:43,547 --> 00:23:44,965
<i>just how very,</i>

390
00:23:45,632 --> 00:23:46,883
<i>very weak</i>

391
00:23:47,801 --> 00:23:49,970
<i>the Steelheart had become.</i>

392
00:23:56,476 --> 00:23:58,437
- Look, um…
- Mm.

393
00:23:59,271 --> 00:24:01,648
Don't cry, no matter what
the doctors might say.

394
00:24:02,732 --> 00:24:05,444
Not your dad.
He doesn't deserve it.

395
00:24:05,944 --> 00:24:08,405
There's no one in the world
as kind as your dad.

396
00:24:09,448 --> 00:24:10,824
Hey, Mom. Mom.

397
00:24:11,825 --> 00:24:12,659
Did you hear me?

398
00:24:13,326 --> 00:24:15,120
No matter how sick he may be,

399
00:24:15,704 --> 00:24:17,289
I'll make sure he gets treated.

400
00:24:17,914 --> 00:24:19,291
Yeah, I believe you.

401
00:24:19,875 --> 00:24:21,209
I believe you.

402
00:24:21,293 --> 00:24:22,919
So don't cry
in front of Dad.

403
00:24:25,172 --> 00:24:27,007
He's feeling a bit of a shock right now.

404
00:24:30,594 --> 00:24:33,346
You've had rheumatoid arthritis
for a long time.

405
00:24:33,847 --> 00:24:36,349
I don't know how you bore
so much pain for so long.

406
00:24:37,058 --> 00:24:39,686
Sometimes, the symptoms of
multiple myeloma are mistaken

407
00:24:39,769 --> 00:24:41,605
for rheumatoid arthritis in joints,

408
00:24:42,147 --> 00:24:44,357
which can delay a correct diagnosis.

409
00:24:44,941 --> 00:24:46,485
Multiple myeloma

410
00:24:47,194 --> 00:24:48,612
is a kind of blood cancer.

411
00:24:48,695 --> 00:24:51,448
Let's call it
a distant relative of leukemia.

412
00:24:52,032 --> 00:24:54,659
<i>He never knew anything</i>
<i>about pop culture.</i>

413
00:24:54,743 --> 00:24:56,995
<i>I was always frustrated with Dad because</i>

414
00:24:57,078 --> 00:25:00,499
<i>every time there was a new girl band,</i>
<i>he'd ask, "Is that Sung Yu-ri?"</i>

415
00:25:01,041 --> 00:25:03,793
<i>Dad just wanted to have</i>
<i>conversations with his daughter.</i>

416
00:25:04,961 --> 00:25:07,005
<i>He also wanted to play the guitar.</i>

417
00:25:07,881 --> 00:25:11,092
<i>But I didn't understand,</i>
<i>or I pretended not to.</i>

418
00:25:11,176 --> 00:25:12,677
People who just bear the pain

419
00:25:12,761 --> 00:25:15,096
actually permit the disease
to develop further.

420
00:25:15,597 --> 00:25:19,351
This has already progressed
to kidney failure, and you didn't know it.

421
00:25:19,434 --> 00:25:21,645
You must've been very tired all the time.

422
00:25:22,229 --> 00:25:23,230
So…

423
00:25:25,941 --> 00:25:26,816
what now?

424
00:25:28,652 --> 00:25:29,736
Well, at this point,

425
00:25:30,695 --> 00:25:32,489
if we start the treatment now,

426
00:25:33,406 --> 00:25:34,908
he could have a slight chance.

427
00:25:36,535 --> 00:25:37,536
But that's about it.

428
00:25:41,915 --> 00:25:44,459
<i>The heavens</i>
<i>were merciless to my dad,</i>

429
00:25:45,627 --> 00:25:48,505
<i>who had just become interested</i>
<i>in Kim Kwang-seok.</i>

430
00:25:51,466 --> 00:25:53,093
Yeah, yeah.

431
00:25:53,802 --> 00:25:55,595
Uh, you don't need to pick him up.

432
00:25:56,263 --> 00:25:59,599
Geum-myeong, he'll be at the hospital
longer than one or two days.

433
00:25:59,683 --> 00:26:00,809
Don't do that.

434
00:26:00,892 --> 00:26:03,645
It'll be too much. Too much for you.

435
00:26:23,039 --> 00:26:23,873
Here.

436
00:26:28,211 --> 00:26:29,713
Don't you worry about it.

437
00:26:30,672 --> 00:26:33,174
We'll get it done.
We'll get what you need.

438
00:26:34,301 --> 00:26:35,802
I'll get the right treatment.

439
00:26:37,762 --> 00:26:38,597
Let's go.

440
00:26:54,070 --> 00:26:56,615
<i>The 24 sessions</i>
<i>of chemotherapy</i>

441
00:26:57,240 --> 00:26:58,825
<i>melted the Steelheart.</i>

442
00:26:59,451 --> 00:27:01,870
<i>Mom even forgot which season it was.</i>

443
00:27:02,871 --> 00:27:06,207
Hey, my angel. Look at the flowers.

444
00:27:08,877 --> 00:27:11,254
Writing poems, you need to enjoy nature.

445
00:27:12,213 --> 00:27:13,340
Have you been writing?

446
00:27:14,758 --> 00:27:16,551
I wanna read your poems.

447
00:27:17,886 --> 00:27:20,847
You love flowers so much,
but you're staring at my feet.

448
00:27:21,348 --> 00:27:23,933
I can't let you fall.

449
00:27:24,893 --> 00:27:25,810
Have a look.

450
00:27:26,645 --> 00:27:27,646
Look at the flowers.

451
00:27:44,579 --> 00:27:48,041
Next year,
let's see the leaves in Zhangjiajie.

452
00:27:48,792 --> 00:27:51,544
The brat Mi-suk went there.
She was showing off.

453
00:27:54,589 --> 00:27:56,591
Why are you holding my hands so tightly?

454
00:27:57,258 --> 00:27:59,302
You think someone's taking me away?

455
00:27:59,386 --> 00:28:00,762
If you leave me,

456
00:28:01,596 --> 00:28:02,722
I'll be alone.

457
00:28:03,306 --> 00:28:04,140
You know that?

458
00:28:04,224 --> 00:28:05,934
You'll never be alone. You have our kids.

459
00:28:06,017 --> 00:28:07,268
Oh, but I don't.

460
00:28:08,311 --> 00:28:10,146
They have their own families now.

461
00:28:12,315 --> 00:28:13,817
A big nuisance.

462
00:28:14,609 --> 00:28:16,236
You see yourself as a nuisance.

463
00:28:17,278 --> 00:28:19,364
When we were young, I'd think about

464
00:28:19,447 --> 00:28:21,866
your uncle not letting you
have croakers at home,

465
00:28:22,450 --> 00:28:24,828
and I'd get so angry I wouldn't be able to

466
00:28:26,371 --> 00:28:27,497
sleep at all.

467
00:28:28,665 --> 00:28:31,793
Ever since then,
you've seen yourself as a nuisance.

468
00:28:34,629 --> 00:28:35,797
So you need to win.

469
00:28:36,798 --> 00:28:40,844
A single mother is nothing
but a nuisance to her children.

470
00:28:42,470 --> 00:28:44,264
Don't make me grow old on my own.

471
00:28:45,432 --> 00:28:46,516
Of course.

472
00:28:46,599 --> 00:28:48,143
I'll never leave you.

473
00:28:52,397 --> 00:28:54,858
I wouldn't dare leave
Ae-sun behind all alone.

474
00:28:56,276 --> 00:28:58,236
<i>The rest of my dad's life</i>

475
00:28:58,319 --> 00:29:00,280
<i>passed like a cherry blossom's.</i>

476
00:29:04,117 --> 00:29:08,496
Oh! That was tough, huh?
Did it make you feel queasy?

477
00:29:08,580 --> 00:29:09,581
Not really.

478
00:29:09,664 --> 00:29:11,040
There was no pain.

479
00:29:11,124 --> 00:29:13,168
It was painful. Don't say it wasn't.

480
00:29:13,668 --> 00:29:15,086
Of course it hurt. How could it not?

481
00:29:15,170 --> 00:29:16,337
Is Yang Gwan-sik here?

482
00:29:17,088 --> 00:29:18,089
Oh, yes, yes.

483
00:29:19,340 --> 00:29:21,509
Drink this, okay? Drink it, okay?

484
00:29:22,302 --> 00:29:24,387
- Mr. Seo Ji-won.
- Yes.

485
00:29:25,847 --> 00:29:27,390
Did you get the blood work done already?

486
00:29:28,183 --> 00:29:32,103
Oh, no, I was told downstairs
to come here first.

487
00:29:32,187 --> 00:29:34,272
The instructions are written right there.

488
00:29:34,856 --> 00:29:36,232
Oh my.

489
00:29:36,316 --> 00:29:38,651
- Please leave.
- Sorry?

490
00:29:38,735 --> 00:29:40,528
- Please go out.
- I'm supposed to be…

491
00:29:40,612 --> 00:29:43,698
You can't just walk in.
You have to put those out here. Here.

492
00:29:43,782 --> 00:29:47,076
- Oh, I, um, didn't see…
- It's written right here.

493
00:29:49,954 --> 00:29:51,790
Ms. Park Gyeong-ja. Come in, please.

494
00:29:58,213 --> 00:30:02,008
Uh, so he can eat meat of any kind?

495
00:30:02,592 --> 00:30:05,678
Someone said it wouldn't actually be
healthy for him to eat it.

496
00:30:05,762 --> 00:30:07,096
Sure, he should eat well.

497
00:30:07,180 --> 00:30:09,349
- Ah.
- Then see you next month.

498
00:30:09,432 --> 00:30:12,685
Well, sir, would moxibustion be
a good thing he should get?

499
00:30:13,478 --> 00:30:16,105
I hear moxibustion would be good for him.

500
00:30:16,189 --> 00:30:19,025
Will you be asking me about
everything on the Internet?

501
00:30:19,526 --> 00:30:20,360
Uh…

502
00:30:27,575 --> 00:30:31,913
Is this not it?
I have number 832.

503
00:30:32,497 --> 00:30:34,541
You can't bring the number
for the payment window

504
00:30:34,624 --> 00:30:36,000
to the reception window.

505
00:30:37,210 --> 00:30:39,754
Oh. So this number is…

506
00:30:39,838 --> 00:30:42,715
- It's written right over there.
- Oh, so it's…

507
00:30:47,679 --> 00:30:49,597
Last call for 835.

508
00:30:51,850 --> 00:30:52,934
Cut us some slack.

509
00:30:53,017 --> 00:30:54,143
Can you, please?

510
00:30:55,019 --> 00:30:56,604
There are a lot of people here.

511
00:30:57,146 --> 00:30:59,732
We didn't know.
Please, would you cut us some slack?

512
00:31:00,608 --> 00:31:02,151
What's wrong?

513
00:31:02,235 --> 00:31:05,363
Why are you sighing?
How dare you sigh in front of people here!

514
00:31:06,155 --> 00:31:08,700
- Oh, my dear.
- Of course, first-timers don't know.

515
00:31:08,783 --> 00:31:10,994
You all give us attitude
and yell at people all day.

516
00:31:11,077 --> 00:31:12,412
Who do you think you are?

517
00:31:12,495 --> 00:31:14,914
You treat us like complete idiots
if we don't follow everything

518
00:31:14,998 --> 00:31:16,875
you already know,
like we're committing a crime.

519
00:31:16,958 --> 00:31:19,544
She's as smart as anyone.
Smarter than you. She is!

520
00:31:19,627 --> 00:31:21,754
- What happened? Mom, what?
- Geum-myeong, hi.

521
00:31:21,838 --> 00:31:24,299
Where have you been? We need you.

522
00:31:24,883 --> 00:31:27,719
Come with us when we visit the hospital.
Promise you will.

523
00:31:27,802 --> 00:31:29,470
You have to. Be here.

524
00:31:32,056 --> 00:31:33,808
It's because Dad's sick.

525
00:31:34,475 --> 00:31:36,686
When you're sick, you get more frustrated.

526
00:31:37,353 --> 00:31:40,732
You get frustrated easily,
even if you only have a migraine.

527
00:31:42,108 --> 00:31:44,319
He's not mad at you, okay?

528
00:31:46,154 --> 00:31:49,866
You think Dad's always on my side,
no matter what?

529
00:31:50,617 --> 00:31:51,492
He's not.

530
00:31:51,993 --> 00:31:53,161
When you and I fight,

531
00:31:53,870 --> 00:31:55,788
Dad will always side with you first.

532
00:31:57,749 --> 00:32:00,501
If I'm his number one,
you're number zero.

533
00:32:01,377 --> 00:32:04,213
I think Dad sees you
as the precious One Ring.

534
00:32:04,297 --> 00:32:06,591
Anyone messes with you,
and they're dead meat.

535
00:32:17,310 --> 00:32:19,896
<i>All Dad saw was Mom.</i>

536
00:32:22,565 --> 00:32:23,816
<i>He saw Mom</i>

537
00:32:24,817 --> 00:32:26,277
<i>who would be sitting here</i>

538
00:32:27,570 --> 00:32:29,030
<i>all alone one day.</i>

539
00:32:38,081 --> 00:32:38,915
Don't bother.

540
00:32:40,166 --> 00:32:42,293
Put me in a four-person room tomorrow.

541
00:32:42,377 --> 00:32:46,130
I didn't get this room for you.
I did it for Mom's peace of mind.

542
00:32:47,006 --> 00:32:47,840
All right?

543
00:32:49,759 --> 00:32:53,388
I wouldn't have booked you
a VIP suite if you got sick.

544
00:32:53,471 --> 00:32:55,431
I guess I lucked out with
you as my daughter.

545
00:32:55,515 --> 00:32:58,226
Then get well soon
and pay me back in other ways.

546
00:32:58,893 --> 00:33:00,812
You can watch Sae-bom for me

547
00:33:01,354 --> 00:33:03,106
and keep scaring my husband.

548
00:33:05,775 --> 00:33:07,860
He's being good to you, isn't he?

549
00:33:08,569 --> 00:33:09,904
The apple of his eye.

550
00:33:18,496 --> 00:33:20,331
So Chung-seop and I will come tomorrow.

551
00:33:20,415 --> 00:33:22,333
- We'll wash your hair.
- You're going?

552
00:33:23,126 --> 00:33:25,294
What? Like me to stay?

553
00:33:25,378 --> 00:33:27,880
You always tell me to go.
Why do you want me to stay?

554
00:33:28,631 --> 00:33:30,883
Sleep here. I'm all alone.

555
00:33:37,348 --> 00:33:40,268
They give the guardian
a pillow in the VIP suite.

556
00:33:40,351 --> 00:33:41,310
Wow, this is nice.

557
00:33:42,645 --> 00:33:44,397
How much is this place?

558
00:33:44,480 --> 00:33:46,441
You can go to Geum-myeong's to wash up.

559
00:33:47,316 --> 00:33:48,901
She'll be staying here tonight.

560
00:33:53,698 --> 00:33:56,659
Crazy, because her mom
didn't have enough to bribe the teacher?

561
00:33:56,743 --> 00:33:59,495
That's how that kid's dad took away
Mom's class presidency?

562
00:33:59,579 --> 00:34:01,956
- That homeroom teacher was a bad man?
- A dick.

563
00:34:02,790 --> 00:34:03,624
A dick.

564
00:34:08,713 --> 00:34:12,050
So Mom head-butted that lady, really?

565
00:34:13,342 --> 00:34:15,470
- Yeah?
- Cracked that motel owner's nose…

566
00:34:15,553 --> 00:34:16,804
Pow! …with her head.

567
00:34:21,726 --> 00:34:23,102
So did you see Mom?

568
00:34:24,228 --> 00:34:26,147
Did you see her lying next to
Dong-myeong's grave?

569
00:34:27,440 --> 00:34:28,274
I did.

570
00:34:29,692 --> 00:34:31,778
I followed her secretly 'cause I believed

571
00:34:32,445 --> 00:34:34,030
maybe she'd dive in the sea.

572
00:34:34,906 --> 00:34:36,407
How did she live through that?

573
00:34:36,949 --> 00:34:38,451
Your Mom was

574
00:34:39,452 --> 00:34:40,828
twenty-eight at the time.

575
00:34:42,747 --> 00:34:43,706
Twenty-eight.

576
00:34:46,626 --> 00:34:48,753
When I asked your mom to marry me,

577
00:34:48,836 --> 00:34:51,756
I promised her I'd either
pay for college on the mainland

578
00:34:53,049 --> 00:34:54,634
or help her become a poet.

579
00:34:56,636 --> 00:34:59,055
I vowed I'd do
one of those things for her,

580
00:35:00,389 --> 00:35:02,391
thinking I wouldn't even fulfill one.

581
00:35:03,518 --> 00:35:05,394
Mom's been writing these days.

582
00:35:06,395 --> 00:35:07,855
I love watching her write.

583
00:35:08,731 --> 00:35:11,234
She won a local writing competition once.

584
00:35:11,818 --> 00:35:14,112
In her high school class, she was first.

585
00:35:15,363 --> 00:35:17,740
That's how exceptional she is.

586
00:35:19,617 --> 00:35:22,078
Mom could've been
so much more than what she is.

587
00:35:26,791 --> 00:35:27,834
Be good to her.

588
00:35:27,917 --> 00:35:29,919
Promise, hmm?

589
00:35:32,046 --> 00:35:34,048
Dad, you're so annoying.

590
00:35:34,549 --> 00:35:37,176
You had me stay behind to tell me this?

591
00:35:39,137 --> 00:35:41,389
I'm sorry to burden you up to the end.

592
00:35:42,265 --> 00:35:44,392
I'm sorry I'm entrusting my bride to you.

593
00:35:45,476 --> 00:35:47,270
Where do you think you're going?

594
00:35:48,354 --> 00:35:49,897
You're not going anywhere.

595
00:35:49,981 --> 00:35:52,692
I don't want you to. I'm still a kid.

596
00:35:53,276 --> 00:35:54,777
You can't go till I'm grown.

597
00:35:55,403 --> 00:35:57,321
Why are you hell-bent on leaving us?

598
00:35:59,115 --> 00:36:01,117
Geum-myeong, having you

599
00:36:02,326 --> 00:36:04,245
as my daughter was like

600
00:36:05,538 --> 00:36:07,039
catching a whale in a dinghy.

601
00:36:07,957 --> 00:36:10,668
You memorized the multiplication table
before anyone else.

602
00:36:10,751 --> 00:36:12,795
You went to Seoul National University.

603
00:36:15,882 --> 00:36:18,134
I had a full heart, yet I was sorry.

604
00:36:19,093 --> 00:36:20,720
I was sorry for you each day.

605
00:36:22,388 --> 00:36:24,515
I am truly sorry to you,

606
00:36:24,599 --> 00:36:25,850
but to your mom…

607
00:36:27,852 --> 00:36:29,353
my guilt is terrible.

608
00:36:32,273 --> 00:36:33,232
It keeps me awake.

609
00:36:34,317 --> 00:36:35,610
I can't sleep.

610
00:36:36,652 --> 00:36:38,863
Stay by Mom's side, then,
if it's that hard.

611
00:36:40,031 --> 00:36:41,866
Just stay with us a bit longer.

612
00:36:43,451 --> 00:36:44,285
Geum-myeong,

613
00:36:45,620 --> 00:36:47,246
you are my baby…

614
00:36:49,749 --> 00:36:51,500
and I'm sorry I'm leaving you.

615
00:36:55,379 --> 00:36:56,339
Your mom

616
00:36:58,257 --> 00:37:00,092
means the world to me, okay?

617
00:37:02,386 --> 00:37:03,721
Don't treat her like

618
00:37:03,804 --> 00:37:05,598
she's being a pain.

619
00:37:06,390 --> 00:37:07,975
Don't get impatient with her,

620
00:37:09,602 --> 00:37:10,770
and be sweet to her.

621
00:37:15,566 --> 00:37:16,442
Treat her well.

622
00:37:21,072 --> 00:37:22,406
How can I…

623
00:37:25,576 --> 00:37:28,621
How can I say goodbye to you? How?

624
00:37:39,006 --> 00:37:40,675
Oh, but Dad,

625
00:37:41,425 --> 00:37:42,802
I'm sorry, Dad.

626
00:37:42,885 --> 00:37:44,512
I'm sorry.

627
00:37:45,304 --> 00:37:48,057
Dad, sorry I get so annoyed. Mm?

628
00:37:49,850 --> 00:37:53,104
Sorry I'm always hanging up on you
and always rushed.

629
00:37:55,273 --> 00:37:59,986
But I was never actually
frustrated with you, you know?

630
00:38:01,612 --> 00:38:03,114
It was never that.

631
00:38:03,197 --> 00:38:04,615
Really, Dad.

632
00:38:09,412 --> 00:38:10,621
I know.

633
00:38:11,998 --> 00:38:13,165
Of course I know.

634
00:38:14,542 --> 00:38:16,502
I have the best daughter in the world.

635
00:38:20,047 --> 00:38:23,050
<i>I had a very loving father.</i>

636
00:38:23,134 --> 00:38:25,886
So tell me,
is Dad coming to see me or not?

637
00:38:27,221 --> 00:38:28,431
<i>But my dad</i>

638
00:38:29,056 --> 00:38:30,641
<i>didn't have a loving daughter.</i>

639
00:38:31,267 --> 00:38:33,644
"A big fish from a small pond."

640
00:38:34,770 --> 00:38:36,564
I really hate that saying.

641
00:38:37,398 --> 00:38:40,693
What good is it that you're a fish
that made it out of the pond?

642
00:38:40,776 --> 00:38:42,403
The pillar, the older sibling.

643
00:38:42,486 --> 00:38:44,780
- God, I'm sick of it all!
- Yang Geum-myeong!

644
00:38:45,781 --> 00:38:48,993
<i>His loving request</i>
<i>for me to be sweet to my mom</i>

645
00:38:50,036 --> 00:38:52,413
<i>still stings in my heart.</i>

646
00:38:52,496 --> 00:38:55,291
You want me to live like you?
Is that what you want?

647
00:38:55,374 --> 00:38:57,460
Yes, because I didn't wanna live like you.

648
00:38:57,960 --> 00:39:00,671
I just couldn't live like
you and mom did. I hated it, you know?

649
00:39:00,755 --> 00:39:04,342
You smelled like cooling patches
every day. What have you done for me?

650
00:39:05,009 --> 00:39:06,427
<i>We treated him</i>

651
00:39:07,845 --> 00:39:09,722
<i>as if we'd have him forever.</i>

652
00:39:11,390 --> 00:39:13,601
Is it okay for him
to be at home?

653
00:39:14,352 --> 00:39:15,519
That's what he'd like.

654
00:39:16,270 --> 00:39:18,773
He says he wants
to live at home for a while.

655
00:39:19,648 --> 00:39:21,025
He wants to see the sea.

656
00:39:22,068 --> 00:39:25,321
It might be better for him
if he stays home with us.

657
00:39:25,404 --> 00:39:26,864
Careful.

658
00:39:39,585 --> 00:39:43,506
Dad, sit on this stationary bike
so your back feels better, okay?

659
00:39:44,173 --> 00:39:47,009
Or you can sit here
and just listen to Kim Kwang-seok.

660
00:39:47,802 --> 00:39:50,763
I also scoured the Internet
and got this vinyl.

661
00:39:51,555 --> 00:39:52,473
Here's a guitar.

662
00:39:56,519 --> 00:39:57,353
Oh, Dad,

663
00:39:58,020 --> 00:39:59,021
how…

664
00:39:59,605 --> 00:40:00,439
how did you…

665
00:40:02,358 --> 00:40:03,734
how did you become so thin?

666
00:40:05,319 --> 00:40:06,362
Dad.

667
00:40:07,655 --> 00:40:08,781
Oh, Dad.

668
00:40:08,864 --> 00:40:10,241
Why, Dad?

669
00:40:10,324 --> 00:40:13,994
Hey, you're a dad yourself now.
You gotta be strong, son.

670
00:40:15,913 --> 00:40:17,415
Dad, why are you doing this?

671
00:40:19,333 --> 00:40:21,293
There's so much I wanted to do for you.

672
00:40:22,378 --> 00:40:24,088
I said I'd buy you a Mercedes.

673
00:40:24,672 --> 00:40:26,340
I wanted to get you another boat.

674
00:40:27,633 --> 00:40:28,843
I've been in one before.

675
00:40:29,427 --> 00:40:30,845
I don't need another one.

676
00:40:33,806 --> 00:40:35,141
You've been a good son.

677
00:40:38,227 --> 00:40:39,186
I already know.

678
00:40:39,854 --> 00:40:41,814
I always knew, but I…

679
00:40:43,315 --> 00:40:44,150
I…

680
00:40:45,985 --> 00:40:49,572
Your brother died
three days after your birthday.

681
00:40:50,072 --> 00:40:51,907
They can't celebrate it, understand?

682
00:40:51,991 --> 00:40:54,034
That's not fair.

683
00:40:54,618 --> 00:40:57,371
I don't wanna!

684
00:41:02,209 --> 00:41:03,794
Eun-myeong, come here.

685
00:41:12,511 --> 00:41:14,180
Eun-myeong, choose one.

686
00:41:14,263 --> 00:41:18,058
We can do some rice cakes at the house
or have sweet and sour pork here.

687
00:41:18,142 --> 00:41:19,768
Can't do both. You can pick only one.

688
00:41:21,145 --> 00:41:22,771
What are you trying?

689
00:41:25,441 --> 00:41:28,027
I'll buy you those secretly then,
or should I not?

690
00:41:30,279 --> 00:41:32,948
Then you'll keep this our secret, yeah?

691
00:41:34,241 --> 00:41:35,910
You're going to tell your sister,

692
00:41:36,702 --> 00:41:37,536
aren't you?

693
00:41:38,037 --> 00:41:39,038
Tattletale.

694
00:41:39,872 --> 00:41:43,709
Sometimes you like me better
than Geum-myeong, I think, Dad.

695
00:41:46,962 --> 00:41:47,796
Have some pork.

696
00:41:47,880 --> 00:41:49,465
<i>You bought that just for me.</i>

697
00:41:50,132 --> 00:41:51,509
And you did it secretly.

698
00:41:52,885 --> 00:41:54,220
I know all that.

699
00:41:57,097 --> 00:41:59,183
See, I do remember the good stuff.

700
00:41:59,266 --> 00:42:00,726
You tattletale.

701
00:42:01,602 --> 00:42:03,020
You're turning me in now?

702
00:42:04,730 --> 00:42:06,065
I'm an asshole.

703
00:42:08,734 --> 00:42:10,986
Oh, now you're bombarding me with insults.

704
00:42:16,825 --> 00:42:18,786
The aunties harvested these.

705
00:42:19,286 --> 00:42:21,914
That damn sea.
It must know I'm angry you're sick.

706
00:42:21,997 --> 00:42:24,124
They were apparently so easy to harvest.

707
00:42:25,918 --> 00:42:27,586
<i>The sea provided endlessly,</i>

708
00:42:27,670 --> 00:42:30,297
<i>no matter how much</i>
<i>we harvested in our lives.</i>

709
00:42:31,298 --> 00:42:33,217
Mom, your son's here.

710
00:42:33,801 --> 00:42:35,052
Wash up quickly.

711
00:42:35,928 --> 00:42:37,263
Wash up and eat.

712
00:42:40,599 --> 00:42:41,559
<i>To us,</i>

713
00:42:42,351 --> 00:42:43,852
<i>Dad was the sea.</i>

714
00:42:46,730 --> 00:42:49,191
<i>We all relied on him to live.</i>

715
00:42:54,572 --> 00:42:56,532
<i>One day,</i>
<i>this petite person brought me</i>

716
00:42:56,615 --> 00:42:59,994
<i>a can of Cherry Coke and offered me</i>
<i>a contract to work with her.</i>

717
00:43:00,619 --> 00:43:02,371
<i>She told me with conviction that…</i>

718
00:43:02,454 --> 00:43:04,707
You see, courses on tape are the future.

719
00:43:05,332 --> 00:43:08,043
<i>Honestly,</i>
<i>I found it ridiculous at first,</i>

720
00:43:08,544 --> 00:43:10,254
<i>but as soon as</i>
<i>I heard of the company name,</i>

721
00:43:10,754 --> 00:43:13,132
<i>I remember thinking I'd give it a chance.</i>

722
00:43:13,882 --> 00:43:16,969
<i>The next speaker</i>
<i>that I will bring to the stage</i>

723
00:43:17,052 --> 00:43:19,680
<i>is someone who is going</i>
<i>to change the industry.</i>

724
00:43:20,472 --> 00:43:23,642
<i>Please welcome the CEO of Ever Study,</i>
<i>Yang Geum-myeong.</i>

725
00:43:25,519 --> 00:43:27,438
TODAY'S NOTABLE LECTURER
YANG GEUM-MYEONG, CEO

726
00:43:27,521 --> 00:43:31,317
Ooh! It's Geum-myeong. It's Geum-myeong.

727
00:43:32,234 --> 00:43:33,986
<i>We had to repay our debt.</i>

728
00:43:34,570 --> 00:43:38,282
<i>We shone the pathway</i>
<i>for a farewell with a fanfare.</i>

729
00:43:38,365 --> 00:43:40,826
Hello, my name is Yang Geum-myeong.

730
00:43:41,785 --> 00:43:43,329
I studied in Japan,

731
00:43:43,912 --> 00:43:47,458
and I used to listen to lectures
over and over again.

732
00:43:48,375 --> 00:43:50,294
<i>Because I couldn't speak the language,</i>

733
00:43:50,794 --> 00:43:52,713
<i>this was all I had to rely on.</i>

734
00:43:54,298 --> 00:43:55,758
<i>I thought to myself,</i>

735
00:43:55,841 --> 00:43:59,261
<i>"Wouldn't it be great if I could</i>
<i>keep the teacher in my pocket?"</i>

736
00:43:59,345 --> 00:44:02,765
One day, I was in my hometown,
staring at the bookcase.

737
00:44:02,848 --> 00:44:03,849
And it

738
00:44:04,600 --> 00:44:05,893
hit like a truck.

739
00:44:07,770 --> 00:44:10,731
I, uh, saw an old workbook

740
00:44:12,316 --> 00:44:14,568
for my mom's college entrance exam.

741
00:44:15,819 --> 00:44:17,780
Is she talking about me?

742
00:44:18,405 --> 00:44:22,076
<i>My mother was exceptional through</i>
<i>every part of her life.</i>

743
00:44:22,159 --> 00:44:24,662
<i>She was smart and diligent,</i>

744
00:44:24,745 --> 00:44:27,039
<i>and she really wanted to pursue</i>

745
00:44:27,748 --> 00:44:29,500
a higher education.

746
00:44:30,084 --> 00:44:33,962
Had my mom been given access
to classes in the palm of her hand,

747
00:44:34,046 --> 00:44:36,215
she could have studied
to her heart's content.

748
00:44:36,882 --> 00:44:38,676
My mom would've thrived.

749
00:44:39,343 --> 00:44:43,430
Even if she never lived in Daechi-dong
and didn't have expensive tutors,

750
00:44:43,514 --> 00:44:47,559
the bookworm on Jeju Island
should've been able to study.

751
00:44:50,104 --> 00:44:52,606
I think anyone who wants to study

752
00:44:53,857 --> 00:44:55,693
should be able to do so,

753
00:44:55,776 --> 00:44:58,737
whoever, whenever, wherever.

754
00:44:59,321 --> 00:45:00,406
Ever Study.

755
00:45:01,699 --> 00:45:03,075
It all began

756
00:45:03,951 --> 00:45:05,452
as my mother's dream.

757
00:45:05,953 --> 00:45:07,287
Her childhood dream.

758
00:45:09,665 --> 00:45:10,666
Aw!

759
00:45:13,210 --> 00:45:14,253
I can't believe it.

760
00:45:15,170 --> 00:45:17,506
I can't believe her.

761
00:45:17,589 --> 00:45:19,800
She's quite the saleswoman there.

762
00:45:22,511 --> 00:45:23,554
<i>And then,</i>

763
00:45:23,637 --> 00:45:27,683
<i>high-speed Internet user numbers</i>
<i>surpassed ten million people.</i>

764
00:45:27,766 --> 00:45:30,227
Tech made video conferencing a reality.

765
00:45:30,310 --> 00:45:33,439
Divided families in North and South Korea
were able to speak again.

766
00:45:34,022 --> 00:45:36,734
I knew the age of online classes
would come one day.

767
00:45:36,817 --> 00:45:40,279
So I seized the possibility
with the persevering spirit

768
00:45:40,362 --> 00:45:41,613
<i>that I inherited from my father.</i>

769
00:45:41,697 --> 00:45:43,198
She mentioned me too. She did.

770
00:45:44,658 --> 00:45:46,160
<i>There were things</i>

771
00:45:46,660 --> 00:45:48,871
<i>that I wanted to show my dad.</i>

772
00:45:49,455 --> 00:45:51,874
<i>Today, the Haenyeo Museum</i>
<i>has opened to celebrate</i>

773
00:45:51,957 --> 00:45:54,084
<i>the pride and the history</i>
<i>of Jeju's </i>haenyeo<i>.</i>

774
00:45:54,168 --> 00:45:55,711
Right here. Perfect. That's great.

775
00:45:55,794 --> 00:45:58,547
<i>By opening this museum</i>
<i>that shows</i>

776
00:45:59,131 --> 00:46:02,509
<i>the pride and the history</i>
<i>of the Jeju </i>haenyeo<i>,</i>

777
00:46:02,593 --> 00:46:07,097
<i>we can show everyone</i>
<i>the world of the </i>haenyeo.

778
00:46:07,181 --> 00:46:10,517
<i>To be included in the list</i>
<i>of World Heritage sites,</i>

779
00:46:10,601 --> 00:46:12,728
<i>we want to show that we have</i>

780
00:46:14,062 --> 00:46:15,522
<i>a living job.</i>

781
00:46:15,606 --> 00:46:16,982
<i>And we are still alive.</i>

782
00:46:17,065 --> 00:46:19,985
<i>Our culture's alive, just as we are.</i>

783
00:46:20,068 --> 00:46:22,696
<i>We want to do our best to revive.</i>

784
00:46:22,780 --> 00:46:24,698
<i>- Preserve, inherit.</i>
- Are you serious?

785
00:46:24,782 --> 00:46:26,742
How can you do this to your dad?

786
00:46:26,825 --> 00:46:29,787
You took cash from my wallet
for an A-reum headband. Really?

787
00:46:29,870 --> 00:46:32,998
It's not A-reum, you know.
It's Jeong A-ram.

788
00:46:33,791 --> 00:46:36,543
Honey, did you do these highlights
on our son?

789
00:46:37,252 --> 00:46:39,630
- Say, "Ah."
- Look at this boy.

790
00:46:40,756 --> 00:46:43,967
You'll go to school with these highlights?
You have a crush on that girl, right?

791
00:46:44,051 --> 00:46:47,679
- Mom and Dad already know.
- Your dad can do it all. Mr. MacGyver.

792
00:46:49,056 --> 00:46:51,183
Dad,
why do you keep laughing?

793
00:46:51,683 --> 00:46:54,019
It's like you laugh
every time I yell at Je-il.

794
00:46:54,102 --> 00:46:56,897
What goes around
comes around, huh?

795
00:46:57,648 --> 00:46:59,900
You always reap what you sow.
Revenge is sweet.

796
00:47:05,614 --> 00:47:06,740
What?

797
00:47:08,826 --> 00:47:10,202
Unbelievable.

798
00:47:12,329 --> 00:47:13,372
Babe.

799
00:47:14,289 --> 00:47:16,583
What? What is it now?

800
00:47:16,667 --> 00:47:18,418
Oh, it's not real.

801
00:47:19,127 --> 00:47:21,088
Why can't we have
a moment's peace in this house?

802
00:47:21,964 --> 00:47:23,090
What is it now?

803
00:47:24,716 --> 00:47:26,301
You kept your word.

804
00:47:26,927 --> 00:47:30,138
The promise. You kept one out of three.

805
00:47:42,442 --> 00:47:45,279
<i>"To the one</i>
<i>who will be leaving me behind."</i>

806
00:47:45,362 --> 00:47:48,365
<i>"Oh Ae-sun of Dodong-dong Jeju."</i>

807
00:47:49,324 --> 00:47:53,036
<i>"When I was young, I thought I had to</i>
<i>hold your hand to feel warmth."</i>

808
00:47:53,912 --> 00:47:55,622
<i>"Now I know you're with me</i>

809
00:47:55,706 --> 00:47:57,457
<i>even when you're not around."</i>

810
00:47:59,001 --> 00:48:01,003
<i>"Now I have a warm floor."</i>

811
00:48:01,879 --> 00:48:04,798
<i>"Just the thought of you warms my heart."</i>

812
00:48:06,550 --> 00:48:09,595
<i>"I will go on knowing</i>
<i>that the moon is in the sky</i>

813
00:48:09,678 --> 00:48:11,179
<i>even during the day."</i>

814
00:48:11,972 --> 00:48:14,266
<i>"So when it's time for you to go,</i>

815
00:48:14,349 --> 00:48:15,934
<i>spread your wings and fly."</i>

816
00:48:16,518 --> 00:48:18,687
<i>"After 50 years, you can fly free."</i>

817
00:48:18,770 --> 00:48:20,647
<i>"You can let me go now."</i>

818
00:48:20,731 --> 00:48:22,524
<i>"My precious love,</i>

819
00:48:22,608 --> 00:48:24,568
<i>I'm eternally thankful to you."</i>

820
00:48:25,152 --> 00:48:26,737
<i>"You showed me what to do</i>

821
00:48:27,237 --> 00:48:29,281
<i>when life gives you tangerines."</i>

822
00:48:37,164 --> 00:48:39,666
You've been crying a lot more lately.

823
00:48:47,674 --> 00:48:50,928
You see? You kept one promise, after all.

824
00:48:52,554 --> 00:48:55,641
Now I'm a published poet, you see?

825
00:48:56,642 --> 00:49:00,062
Yeah, but if you weren't with me,
it wouldn't have taken so long.

826
00:49:00,646 --> 00:49:02,898
I couldn't be doing it without you.

827
00:49:02,981 --> 00:49:05,233
I couldn't write poems like this.

828
00:49:06,735 --> 00:49:07,819
Ah, well.

829
00:49:08,320 --> 00:49:09,571
Damn it, Ae-sun.

830
00:49:09,655 --> 00:49:11,448
Damn it, Ae-sun.

831
00:49:14,576 --> 00:49:15,410
You thrilled?

832
00:49:17,412 --> 00:49:18,747
Oh yes.

833
00:49:20,207 --> 00:49:21,041
This is

834
00:49:21,875 --> 00:49:23,043
everything.

835
00:49:29,466 --> 00:49:31,510
Grandma and Grandpa are kissing.

836
00:49:32,594 --> 00:49:33,595
Oh. Piggyback?

837
00:49:33,679 --> 00:49:35,472
- Get on.
- I'm heavy.

838
00:49:35,555 --> 00:49:37,891
- Hey, my kids are watching. Be careful.
- You sure? Careful.

839
00:49:37,975 --> 00:49:40,102
If you and Mom keep doing that,
they'll think romance is

840
00:49:40,185 --> 00:49:41,561
the best thing in the world.

841
00:49:42,229 --> 00:49:46,108
Hey, buy a hundred of Mom's books
and give them to the fishing village.

842
00:49:46,191 --> 00:49:47,109
You have to.

843
00:49:52,197 --> 00:49:54,282
<i>She wanted time</i>
<i>to stop that day.</i>

844
00:49:54,783 --> 00:49:56,910
<i>She wanted the bonus track to never end.</i>

845
00:49:58,245 --> 00:50:01,331
<i>Mom wanted that night to last forever.</i>

846
00:50:07,421 --> 00:50:08,672
Honey.

847
00:50:10,132 --> 00:50:11,883
Can we keep living like this?

848
00:50:13,635 --> 00:50:15,262
I'd love it if we could get

849
00:50:15,846 --> 00:50:17,806
five more years together.

850
00:50:22,227 --> 00:50:23,103
Or

851
00:50:24,730 --> 00:50:26,314
at least one more year.

852
00:50:27,524 --> 00:50:29,985
To experience seasons, okay?

853
00:50:30,485 --> 00:50:32,738
I thought I may not be able to fulfill

854
00:50:33,780 --> 00:50:35,282
even one of the three.

855
00:50:36,033 --> 00:50:37,909
Now that you're writing poems again,

856
00:50:39,369 --> 00:50:40,871
I feel much better.

857
00:50:41,872 --> 00:50:42,873
Much better.

858
00:50:44,207 --> 00:50:45,876
In my next life,

859
00:50:47,627 --> 00:50:50,630
I'll do five, ten promises.

860
00:50:53,258 --> 00:50:54,509
Wanna be there with me?

861
00:51:01,683 --> 00:51:02,893
You believe

862
00:51:04,561 --> 00:51:05,896
we'll meet there?

863
00:51:07,272 --> 00:51:08,106
Why?

864
00:51:09,316 --> 00:51:10,776
Don't wanna be there with me?

865
00:51:16,406 --> 00:51:18,408
Such blessings

866
00:51:18,492 --> 00:51:19,910
don't come easily.

867
00:51:22,162 --> 00:51:24,873
Others deserve a chance
to live the good life.

868
00:51:27,876 --> 00:51:30,587
It's my fault you suffered
your entire life.

869
00:51:32,547 --> 00:51:34,132
I was never lonely

870
00:51:35,675 --> 00:51:37,427
because of you, dear.

871
00:51:39,805 --> 00:51:40,806
Not a day.

872
00:51:43,767 --> 00:51:45,769
It was a wonderful life.

873
00:51:48,063 --> 00:51:48,897
Ae-sun.

874
00:51:49,815 --> 00:51:50,649
Huh?

875
00:51:51,233 --> 00:51:52,984
I have one thing to ask of you.

876
00:51:56,655 --> 00:51:57,823
Don't weep a lot…

877
00:51:59,908 --> 00:52:01,034
when the time's near.

878
00:52:03,495 --> 00:52:05,122
It's always hard for me

879
00:52:06,623 --> 00:52:08,041
when you weep like that.

880
00:52:11,169 --> 00:52:13,004
I'd never be able to fly away.

881
00:52:15,674 --> 00:52:17,008
What I wanna see…

882
00:52:19,094 --> 00:52:21,638
What I really wanna see
in my last minutes…

883
00:52:24,850 --> 00:52:26,309
is your smile.

884
00:52:28,770 --> 00:52:30,188
Life was full of joy

885
00:52:31,565 --> 00:52:33,733
'cause of your beautiful laughter, Ae-sun.

886
00:52:44,119 --> 00:52:45,579
Hey.

887
00:52:46,121 --> 00:52:48,415
You can't even do that?

888
00:52:51,084 --> 00:52:52,544
Pat me on the back.

889
00:53:06,600 --> 00:53:08,185
<i>♪ Sleep ♪</i>

890
00:53:08,685 --> 00:53:09,769
<i>♪ Sleep ♪</i>

891
00:53:12,689 --> 00:53:14,941
<i>♪ Sweet child ♪</i>

892
00:53:16,902 --> 00:53:17,986
<i>♪ Sleep ♪</i>

893
00:53:18,570 --> 00:53:22,574
<i>♪ Sleep, sweet child, rest ♪</i>

894
00:53:25,660 --> 00:53:31,166
<i>♪ My baby is fast asleep ♪</i>

895
00:53:33,376 --> 00:53:35,837
<i>♪ Sleep now ♪</i>

896
00:53:35,921 --> 00:53:37,797
<i>♪ Sleep now ♪</i>

897
00:53:40,217 --> 00:53:43,053
<i>♪ Little black dog ♪</i>

898
00:53:43,136 --> 00:53:45,388
<i>♪ As you go ♪</i>

899
00:53:46,640 --> 00:53:49,768
<i>♪ Little black dog ♪</i>

900
00:53:50,268 --> 00:53:52,604
<i>♪ As you come ♪</i>

901
00:53:53,730 --> 00:53:58,485
<i>♪ Help my baby sleep well ♪</i>

902
00:54:00,237 --> 00:54:05,784
<i>♪ I'll help your babies sleep well ♪</i>

903
00:54:06,785 --> 00:54:09,120
<i>Mom always said</i>
<i>she had hard days,</i>

904
00:54:09,788 --> 00:54:11,790
<i>but she never had lonely ones.</i>

905
00:54:11,873 --> 00:54:14,793
<i>In hindsight, my mother lived in paradise.</i>

906
00:54:14,876 --> 00:54:16,962
Oh, wow. Wow, that's terrific.

907
00:54:17,837 --> 00:54:20,757
<i>My dad spent all his life</i>
<i>patting us on our backs.</i>

908
00:54:22,342 --> 00:54:26,179
{\an8}<i>He did his best for us</i>
<i>with all the strength he had in him.</i>

909
00:54:26,263 --> 00:54:28,640
{\an8}<i>Sweetie,</i>
<i>you'll have an accident.</i>

910
00:54:28,723 --> 00:54:30,850
{\an8}<i>Why don't you pull over somewhere?</i>
<i>I'll be right there.</i>

911
00:54:30,934 --> 00:54:32,560
{\an8}It's okay.

912
00:54:33,436 --> 00:54:35,438
{\an8}There aren't any cars.

913
00:54:35,522 --> 00:54:37,857
- There aren't any cars on the road.
<i>- No cars?</i>

914
00:54:38,942 --> 00:54:42,362
Dad, don't go
before I see you. Not before then.

915
00:54:42,862 --> 00:54:45,448
<i>Heaven showed us mercy</i>
<i>one last time.</i>

916
00:54:45,532 --> 00:54:47,867
- <i>So that we could escort him there.</i>
- I'm here.

917
00:54:47,951 --> 00:54:50,036
I'm here, Dad. Dad, I'm right here.

918
00:54:50,537 --> 00:54:51,371
Dad.

919
00:54:51,871 --> 00:54:54,749
Dad, I'm right here. Dad, don't be scared.

920
00:54:54,833 --> 00:54:56,084
Don't be scared, okay?

921
00:54:56,584 --> 00:54:58,962
I'm sorry, Dad.

922
00:54:59,838 --> 00:55:02,299
Dad, Dad, Dad, I love you.

923
00:55:02,382 --> 00:55:05,135
- I'm sorry, Dad. Dad.
- Dad, I love you.

924
00:55:06,386 --> 00:55:08,013
- Dad.
- Honey.

925
00:55:08,096 --> 00:55:09,556
Dad, I'm sorry.

926
00:55:10,557 --> 00:55:14,602
<i>The last look</i>
<i>that Dad got to see on our faces</i>

927
00:55:15,186 --> 00:55:16,521
<i>was a sadness</i>

928
00:55:17,272 --> 00:55:19,024
<i>he'd never seen before.</i>

929
00:55:52,015 --> 00:55:54,351
<i>You should've been easier on yourself.</i>

930
00:55:54,851 --> 00:55:56,478
<i>You've grown old so fast.</i>

931
00:55:58,688 --> 00:56:00,565
<i>But you're still the same.</i>

932
00:56:04,194 --> 00:56:05,820
<i>I've grown old too.</i>

933
00:56:08,239 --> 00:56:09,532
<i>No.</i>

934
00:56:10,116 --> 00:56:11,284
<i>You're the same.</i>

935
00:56:13,203 --> 00:56:15,288
<i>In my eyes, you've never changed</i>

936
00:56:16,373 --> 00:56:17,665
<i>in 50 years.</i>

937
00:56:30,553 --> 00:56:34,057
<i>There was a girl</i>
<i>in a boy's life.</i>

938
00:56:36,768 --> 00:56:38,603
<i>He spent all his life</i>

939
00:56:39,145 --> 00:56:41,356
<i>keeping the girl's world safe.</i>

940
00:56:43,900 --> 00:56:44,859
<i>Thank you,</i>

941
00:56:45,652 --> 00:56:46,486
<i>honey.</i>

942
00:56:48,238 --> 00:56:50,573
<i>You lived a good life.</i>

943
00:56:51,533 --> 00:56:53,410
<i>We had a good life.</i>

944
00:56:57,539 --> 00:56:58,706
<i>Was it good?</i>

945
00:57:01,751 --> 00:57:05,088
<i>Was your life with me any good?</i>

946
00:57:07,257 --> 00:57:09,342
<i>I didn't need anything else.</i>

947
00:57:18,101 --> 00:57:20,937
<i>It was so good</i>
<i>that I didn't need anything more.</i>

948
00:57:24,065 --> 00:57:28,611
<i>As he looked into the eyes</i>
<i>of the one who was ingrained in his soul…</i>

949
00:57:34,659 --> 00:57:37,620
<i>Dad slept in for the first time.</i>

950
00:57:49,090 --> 00:57:50,633
<i>He left many gifts behind.</i>

951
00:57:54,429 --> 00:57:56,973
Your dad wanted you to have this.

952
00:58:01,936 --> 00:58:03,771
<i>Through all these years,</i>

953
00:58:04,397 --> 00:58:05,732
<i>Dad never spent</i>

954
00:58:06,357 --> 00:58:08,943
<i>any of the money I sent him and Mom.</i>

955
00:58:09,027 --> 00:58:11,154
He never withdrew
from this account,

956
00:58:11,237 --> 00:58:13,531
but he would always
check up on it here and there.

957
00:58:14,032 --> 00:58:15,408
He said it made him so happy

958
00:58:15,492 --> 00:58:17,785
that his daughter
could manage sending that much money.

959
00:58:19,537 --> 00:58:21,498
Oh, why didn't he use it?

960
00:58:21,581 --> 00:58:23,082
When you sent 100,000 won,

961
00:58:23,166 --> 00:58:26,085
he said he'd feel a joy
worth a million won.

962
00:58:29,047 --> 00:58:30,256
But all he had

963
00:58:31,174 --> 00:58:32,967
was one closet to his name.

964
00:58:35,303 --> 00:58:37,889
God, Dad, why are you so annoying?

965
00:58:37,972 --> 00:58:41,100
<i>Dad's unrequited love</i>
<i>was now over,</i>

966
00:58:41,184 --> 00:58:42,936
<i>but mine had just begun.</i>

967
00:58:49,526 --> 00:58:51,945
Your father wanted you
to have a Mercedes.

968
00:58:52,779 --> 00:58:55,949
He wanted you to live a great life.

969
00:58:57,867 --> 00:59:00,245
Hmm. What's the odometer read?

970
00:59:02,872 --> 00:59:03,873
That's crazy.

971
00:59:04,791 --> 00:59:07,627
You are so similar to my daughter.

972
00:59:23,184 --> 00:59:24,644
You wear those hairpins every day,

973
00:59:24,727 --> 00:59:26,563
and I keep looking for them all the time.

974
00:59:26,646 --> 00:59:29,607
Why do I bother buying them for you?
You keep losing them anyway.

975
00:59:57,594 --> 01:00:01,389
<i>There was a 50-year love</i>
<i>on Mom's Treasure Island.</i>

976
01:00:18,281 --> 01:00:19,574
<i>It was a love</i>

977
01:00:20,283 --> 01:00:21,826
<i>that would never die.</i>

978
01:00:34,797 --> 01:00:36,591
What am I supposed to do?

979
01:00:40,887 --> 01:00:42,347
How do I go on?

980
01:01:05,620 --> 01:01:07,538
Stop making rolled omelets.

981
01:01:09,999 --> 01:01:12,460
You never could eat <i>sujebi</i>
after Dong-myeong left us.

982
01:01:13,503 --> 01:01:15,672
You might cry
seeing rolled omelets when I'm gone.

983
01:01:35,858 --> 01:01:38,820
If the kids want you
to live with them, go.

984
01:01:38,903 --> 01:01:40,279
That's what I'd want.

985
01:01:41,698 --> 01:01:43,282
If you have to live without me,

986
01:01:43,950 --> 01:01:45,284
don't do it alone.

987
01:02:19,110 --> 01:02:20,027
Oh.

988
01:02:21,237 --> 01:02:23,489
When did he take these down?

989
01:02:40,423 --> 01:02:41,674
Boy, my love

990
01:02:42,759 --> 01:02:44,302
was so busy.

991
01:02:45,970 --> 01:02:47,472
<i>Just as we know</i>

992
01:02:47,555 --> 01:02:50,600
<i>the moon is somewhere in the sky</i>
<i>during the day,</i>

993
01:02:50,683 --> 01:02:53,227
<i>Mom knew Dad was always there.</i>

994
01:03:03,738 --> 01:03:08,367
{\an8}SEEING A LOVED ONE RETURN EACH DAY
THROUGH THE DOOR THEY LEFT IN THE MORNING.

995
01:03:08,451 --> 01:03:12,663
{\an8}IT WAS LIKE A MIRACLE EVERY DAY.

996
01:03:22,673 --> 01:03:24,133
I've written a lot.

997
01:03:26,010 --> 01:03:27,595
So many poems.

998
01:03:33,476 --> 01:03:35,311
Let's have another go.

999
01:03:39,106 --> 01:03:41,108
OH AE-SUN

1000
01:03:44,362 --> 01:03:46,906
<i>Just as white snow</i>
<i>covers the earth,</i>

1001
01:03:47,615 --> 01:03:50,243
<i>time covers all the noise and sorrow.</i>

1002
01:03:53,287 --> 01:03:55,540
<i>Winter had finally arrived.</i>

1003
01:03:58,376 --> 01:03:59,794
I'll be back.

1004
01:04:00,962 --> 01:04:02,338
I'll see you again.

1005
01:04:12,306 --> 01:04:13,516
You see, sir,

1006
01:04:14,100 --> 01:04:17,603
that's just where my husband is,
right there.

1007
01:04:28,155 --> 01:04:29,073
Have a look.

1008
01:04:29,866 --> 01:04:31,742
I did write the entire thing.

1009
01:04:32,326 --> 01:04:33,452
I finished.

1010
01:04:38,583 --> 01:04:41,210
<i>I believe their story</i>
<i>should never be forgotten.</i>

1011
01:04:41,294 --> 01:04:44,463
<i>I'm sending you the 70-year story</i>
<i>of my parents' lives.</i>

1012
01:04:44,547 --> 01:04:48,926
<i>From Yang Geum-myeong, the eldest child of</i>
<i>Yang Gwan-sik and Oh Ae-sun.</i>

1013
01:04:49,427 --> 01:04:52,054
<i>♪ …though they're here to stay ♪</i>

1014
01:04:52,138 --> 01:04:54,599
<i>♪ Oh, I believe ♪</i>

1015
01:04:54,682 --> 01:04:57,393
<i>♪ In yesterday ♪</i>

1016
01:04:57,476 --> 01:04:59,604
<i>♪ Suddenly… ♪</i>

1017
01:05:00,438 --> 01:05:05,651
You know, the things that you've
most wanted to say inside.

1018
01:05:05,735 --> 01:05:09,405
<i>♪ There's a shadow hanging over me ♪</i>

1019
01:05:09,488 --> 01:05:14,577
<i>♪ Oh, yesterday came suddenly ♪</i>

1020
01:05:14,660 --> 01:05:19,165
<i>♪ Why she had to go ♪</i>

1021
01:05:19,248 --> 01:05:21,751
<i>♪ I don't know, she wouldn't say… ♪</i>

1022
01:05:21,834 --> 01:05:25,421
Excuse me, Teacher Ae-sun.
Can you color this for me?

1023
01:05:26,005 --> 01:05:30,134
Jeez, why do you keep
asking me to do things for you?

1024
01:05:30,217 --> 01:05:32,428
It's time you start doing it alone.

1025
01:05:33,804 --> 01:05:36,307
Learn to draw by yourself

1026
01:05:36,933 --> 01:05:38,893
and speak to yourself.

1027
01:05:38,976 --> 01:05:40,728
Play some cards alone

1028
01:05:41,395 --> 01:05:43,439
so you don't become sick.

1029
01:05:44,315 --> 01:05:46,400
You get sick when you're lonely.

1030
01:05:47,234 --> 01:05:50,529
Jeez, why do you keep giving me yours?

1031
01:05:50,613 --> 01:05:51,614
I went

1032
01:05:52,490 --> 01:05:56,410
to your restaurant
with my daughter and her husband.

1033
01:05:56,494 --> 01:05:58,496
I ordered the food myself.

1034
01:05:58,579 --> 01:05:59,956
It's 'cause of you.

1035
01:06:00,790 --> 01:06:03,751
"Jeong Gong-rye, the Illiterate Woman."

1036
01:06:03,834 --> 01:06:06,087
I've been embarrassed all my life

1037
01:06:06,170 --> 01:06:09,215
that I didn't go to school
because I was a <i>haenyeo</i>.

1038
01:06:09,715 --> 01:06:13,678
When anyone asked me
to order something from the menu,

1039
01:06:13,761 --> 01:06:16,097
my heart sank every time.

1040
01:06:16,180 --> 01:06:20,977
But yesterday, I ordered
what I wanted to eat all by myself.

1041
01:06:21,519 --> 01:06:23,396
I ordered a big plate of sushi.

1042
01:06:23,479 --> 01:06:26,524
It was the best thing that I ever had.

1043
01:06:26,607 --> 01:06:27,984
Teacher Ae-sun,

1044
01:06:29,318 --> 01:06:30,236
have a little.

1045
01:06:30,319 --> 01:06:33,197
- Here.
- Oh, why do you keep giving me things?

1046
01:06:33,781 --> 01:06:36,033
You're pretty. You are.

1047
01:06:36,117 --> 01:06:38,202
Do I remind you of your daughter again?

1048
01:06:39,453 --> 01:06:44,542
Oh, how I would have loved it to see
my daughter work at a desk just like you.

1049
01:06:44,625 --> 01:06:46,085
It would be great, my dear,

1050
01:06:46,168 --> 01:06:49,255
if you could earn a living at a desk
like your teacher in elementary school.

1051
01:06:53,384 --> 01:06:54,427
Mm.

1052
01:06:55,928 --> 01:06:59,265
<i>I wish my mother</i>
<i>was here to peel these tangerines.</i>

1053
01:06:59,348 --> 01:07:02,059
<i>I wanna eat a big plate of sushi too.</i>

1054
01:07:03,060 --> 01:07:06,564
<i>The word I wanted to say</i>
<i>again the most in my life</i>…

1055
01:07:07,982 --> 01:07:08,941
Mom.

1056
01:07:11,235 --> 01:07:12,319
Mom.

1057
01:07:13,320 --> 01:07:14,697
Mom!

1058
01:07:16,282 --> 01:07:18,451
Mom!

1059
01:07:21,412 --> 01:07:23,873
Other people live to 90 and 100 years.

1060
01:07:24,457 --> 01:07:26,250
Why were you so eager to go?

1061
01:07:26,959 --> 01:07:29,503
Were you reborn into a better life?

1062
01:07:30,463 --> 01:07:32,673
I hope that you get to work at a desk

1063
01:07:32,757 --> 01:07:35,176
like you wanted, to boss people around.

1064
01:07:42,099 --> 01:07:43,100
MY DAUGHTER

1065
01:07:45,644 --> 01:07:46,562
Hi.

1066
01:07:46,645 --> 01:07:48,147
How am I?

1067
01:07:49,607 --> 01:07:52,943
Well, same ol', same ol', you know.

1068
01:07:54,278 --> 01:07:55,112
What?

1069
01:07:56,947 --> 01:07:58,032
Oh, but why now?

1070
01:08:01,035 --> 01:08:03,079
You said
you couldn't come this month.

1071
01:08:03,162 --> 01:08:07,750
Jeez, I shouldn't have given
the sour kimchi to your aunt.

1072
01:08:08,250 --> 01:08:11,462
Hey, Mom, stop it and just come sit down.

1073
01:08:11,545 --> 01:08:14,548
- Sit down now.
- You like it sour?

1074
01:08:14,632 --> 01:08:17,093
Eun-myeong likes to have it fresh.

1075
01:08:17,176 --> 01:08:19,386
I always have to have those separate.

1076
01:08:20,346 --> 01:08:21,305
Oh my God.

1077
01:08:21,806 --> 01:08:24,475
<i>Mom had been lonely</i>
<i>up until the day before,</i>

1078
01:08:24,558 --> 01:08:27,061
<i>but she turned into that young girl again.</i>

1079
01:08:28,646 --> 01:08:31,524
<i>Their boat was full once again.</i>

1080
01:08:35,444 --> 01:08:37,863
Mother, look, Lim Young-woong is on.

1081
01:08:41,450 --> 01:08:42,576
Oh my.

1082
01:08:47,206 --> 01:08:50,292
Mom, why are you
so into Lim Young-woong?

1083
01:08:51,752 --> 01:08:54,046
Your father loved Kim Kwang-seok.

1084
01:08:54,630 --> 01:08:57,174
He learned guitar
so he could play this song.

1085
01:08:57,675 --> 01:09:00,636
But he never sang it for me because

1086
01:09:01,387 --> 01:09:02,555
he thought he'd cry.

1087
01:09:03,514 --> 01:09:05,766
But now Young-woong is singing it.

1088
01:09:07,977 --> 01:09:08,853
Aw!

1089
01:09:09,353 --> 01:09:10,563
It's a beautiful song.

1090
01:09:12,356 --> 01:09:15,359
Mom,
how do you stay young like that?

1091
01:09:16,318 --> 01:09:18,988
<i>She was still</i>
<i>like a fragile flower petal.</i>

1092
01:09:19,071 --> 01:09:20,781
HAENYEO MUSEUM

1093
01:09:20,865 --> 01:09:24,827
UNESCO INTANGIBLE CULTURAL HERITAGE
HAENYEO PERFORMANCE - LET'S GO TOGETHER

1094
01:09:25,828 --> 01:09:27,872
<i>And she still had dreams.</i>

1095
01:09:29,456 --> 01:09:31,333
Let's go to the hospital together.

1096
01:09:31,917 --> 01:09:33,752
You don't need favors from our kids.

1097
01:09:34,253 --> 01:09:36,505
If you get sick, I'll take care of you.

1098
01:09:37,631 --> 01:09:40,384
Better that you take
a bit more care for yourself.

1099
01:09:40,968 --> 01:09:42,970
What are you doing about that belly?

1100
01:09:43,679 --> 01:09:45,389
The kids are already judging you.

1101
01:09:45,472 --> 01:09:48,350
And you should dye your hair. God.

1102
01:09:50,227 --> 01:09:51,270
Dye it?

1103
01:09:52,479 --> 01:09:53,981
Will you help me?

1104
01:09:56,358 --> 01:09:59,945
So is there an age limit to first love?

1105
01:10:00,029 --> 01:10:02,239
God, stop talking, please.

1106
01:10:03,032 --> 01:10:06,118
- If there isn't, I was wondering if we…
- All right, let me out. Let me out.

1107
01:10:06,202 --> 01:10:08,370
But the car is moving.
How can you ask that?

1108
01:10:08,871 --> 01:10:10,664
Keep driving. Eyes on the road.

1109
01:10:11,999 --> 01:10:14,251
I'm not
your chauffeur now, am I?

1110
01:10:15,169 --> 01:10:17,421
<i>In a season</i>
<i>of unchanging youth,</i>

1111
01:10:19,006 --> 01:10:22,551
<i>my mom still dyed her nails</i>
<i>with crushed balsam flowers.</i>

1112
01:10:23,093 --> 01:10:23,969
Oh.

1113
01:10:25,679 --> 01:10:27,389
You never age, do you?

1114
01:10:29,975 --> 01:10:31,602
What's the big deal with aging?

1115
01:10:31,685 --> 01:10:36,065
Did you feel any different
going from your thirties to your forties?

1116
01:10:36,148 --> 01:10:38,192
You feel the same at your age?

1117
01:10:38,275 --> 01:10:40,110
Oh, exhausting.

1118
01:10:40,945 --> 01:10:42,404
It's the same.

1119
01:10:43,280 --> 01:10:45,699
It's the same.

1120
01:10:47,117 --> 01:10:48,619
You feel the same inside,

1121
01:10:50,579 --> 01:10:52,373
but when you look in the mirror,

1122
01:10:53,457 --> 01:10:55,542
an old woman stares at you.

1123
01:10:56,126 --> 01:10:57,878
That's all aging is.

1124
01:10:57,962 --> 01:11:00,297
Mom. It's here! It's here!

1125
01:11:01,215 --> 01:11:02,758
It wasn't a scam, you see?

1126
01:11:03,259 --> 01:11:04,802
SEAFLOWER PUBLISHERS

1127
01:11:05,386 --> 01:11:07,888
I made it very clear to her
that my sister is successful

1128
01:11:07,972 --> 01:11:09,765
and that I own a franchise.

1129
01:11:09,848 --> 01:11:12,226
I thought the publisher
would charge us more

1130
01:11:12,309 --> 01:11:14,895
just because I wanted to publish
a poem collection so quickly.

1131
01:11:14,979 --> 01:11:16,272
It was very last minute.

1132
01:11:17,022 --> 01:11:19,024
But it wasn't a scam, you see?

1133
01:11:19,984 --> 01:11:22,236
Oh, this is just unbelievable.

1134
01:11:23,862 --> 01:11:26,198
Oh Ae-sun's poem collection.

1135
01:11:27,157 --> 01:11:28,158
Mom,

1136
01:11:29,326 --> 01:11:33,580
I bet Dad is laughing at you now,
isn't he?

1137
01:11:37,293 --> 01:11:39,378
Huh? Grandma's crying again?

1138
01:11:44,842 --> 01:11:46,635
HERE'S TO ALL YOU'VE BEEN THROUGH

1139
01:11:47,136 --> 01:11:47,970
{\an8}TRIBUTE

1140
01:11:48,053 --> 01:11:50,556
{\an8}THE BEAUTIFUL, DREAMLIKE STORY
BROUGHT ME TO TEARS

1141
01:11:50,639 --> 01:11:52,349
{\an8}"I'M SORRY. THANK YOU. I LOVE YOU"

1142
01:11:52,433 --> 01:11:53,267
{\an8}EDITOR'S NOTE

1143
01:12:01,859 --> 01:12:06,780
MENTAL AND FINANCIAL COMPETENCE

1144
01:12:10,576 --> 01:12:14,371
So you're here to see the flowers today.
How do you feel about it?

1145
01:12:14,455 --> 01:12:16,874
Well, the flowers
remind me of my first love.

1146
01:12:16,957 --> 01:12:18,042
Your first love.

1147
01:12:18,125 --> 01:12:20,419
- Of course, yes.
- Go live with her, then.

1148
01:12:21,253 --> 01:12:23,505
Hye-ran. No, no. That's dirty.

1149
01:12:29,803 --> 01:12:33,057
Excuse me, ma'am.
Don't stand there.

1150
01:12:34,099 --> 01:12:36,727
Ma'am, who did you come here to see?

1151
01:12:36,810 --> 01:12:38,937
Well, my mother-in-law
said to pick the pretty lady.

1152
01:12:39,605 --> 01:12:43,025
So which of us would it be? Which one?

1153
01:13:01,210 --> 01:13:03,337
LITTLE PUNK

1154
01:13:05,547 --> 01:13:06,799
THE DAY WE BECAME THE SAME AGE

1155
01:13:06,882 --> 01:13:08,133
I WAS TEN WHEN I LOST MOTHER

1156
01:13:08,217 --> 01:13:10,052
SHE LEFT BEHIND HER THREE CHILDREN AT 29

1157
01:13:10,135 --> 01:13:12,137
WHEN I TURNED 29,
I CRIED LIKE I WAS TEN AGAIN

1158
01:13:50,092 --> 01:13:50,926
Hey.

1159
01:13:51,760 --> 01:13:52,886
Are you crying?

1160
01:13:57,641 --> 01:13:59,059
Oh, what's happening?

1161
01:14:00,727 --> 01:14:02,354
Why is this making me cry?

1162
01:14:04,314 --> 01:14:05,482
Is it that good?

1163
01:14:06,984 --> 01:14:07,943
It's just

1164
01:14:09,236 --> 01:14:10,070
that I'm…

1165
01:14:11,572 --> 01:14:12,406
I'm…

1166
01:14:16,535 --> 01:14:17,911
How can I say it?

1167
01:14:20,789 --> 01:14:21,748
Proud of her.

1168
01:14:23,083 --> 01:14:24,585
So proud.

1169
01:14:27,546 --> 01:14:29,465
OH AE-SUN

1170
01:14:29,548 --> 01:14:30,382
{\an8}CONTENTS

1171
01:14:30,466 --> 01:14:32,676
{\an8}SPRING IN A HEARTBEAT
THE BLAZING SUMMER SUNSHINE

1172
01:14:33,260 --> 01:14:35,804
Should we do something
for your debut publication?

1173
01:14:37,389 --> 01:14:39,766
Can you at least pretend
you want something?

1174
01:14:39,850 --> 01:14:43,812
Your daughter's doing quite well now.
I even bought you your house.

1175
01:14:44,354 --> 01:14:46,231
See me more.

1176
01:14:46,315 --> 01:14:49,359
I want to see my busy daughter at least

1177
01:14:49,443 --> 01:14:52,279
a hundred more times before I go.

1178
01:14:54,573 --> 01:14:56,617
Why would you say that?

1179
01:14:58,327 --> 01:14:59,745
I get to see you

1180
01:15:00,287 --> 01:15:02,456
maybe ten times a year.

1181
01:15:04,458 --> 01:15:07,461
So I'd like to see you
a hundred times a year.

1182
01:15:11,089 --> 01:15:13,342
So you should move to Seoul with me.

1183
01:15:14,051 --> 01:15:16,261
Why do you go to
the nursing home that often?

1184
01:15:18,764 --> 01:15:21,391
You still need a calling in the world.

1185
01:15:21,475 --> 01:15:23,393
It's important at my age.

1186
01:15:23,477 --> 01:15:26,271
I hate being treated
like I'm a waste of space.

1187
01:15:26,855 --> 01:15:29,358
I'd just be relaxing mostly
in that situation.

1188
01:15:30,275 --> 01:15:33,070
You were so, so busy your entire life.

1189
01:15:34,071 --> 01:15:35,364
I only go 'cause

1190
01:15:35,948 --> 01:15:37,616
I get excited doing that.

1191
01:15:39,660 --> 01:15:42,955
See, when I'm there,
"Teacher Ae-sun" is what I'm called.

1192
01:15:43,956 --> 01:15:48,210
Basically, I'm moving up
quite a lot in this world.

1193
01:15:52,714 --> 01:15:56,635
<i>Once, I was a </i>haenyeo's <i>daughter</i>
<i>who cried every day at sea,</i>

1194
01:15:57,219 --> 01:16:01,431
<i>then a bookworm who was so embarrassed</i>
<i>about everything in the world.</i>

1195
01:16:01,515 --> 01:16:04,518
We have a house and a boat.

1196
01:16:05,185 --> 01:16:08,605
<i>Then the most excited</i>
<i>and elated wife of a boat captain.</i>

1197
01:16:11,400 --> 01:16:13,110
<i>Village Chief Oh,</i>

1198
01:16:13,777 --> 01:16:16,613
<i>the fish-filleting lady at the market…</i>

1199
01:16:16,697 --> 01:16:18,156
Crazy, right? And then I was chosen.

1200
01:16:18,240 --> 01:16:20,284
<i>Supposedly a teacher at 70,</i>

1201
01:16:20,367 --> 01:16:22,828
<i>and now, Oh Ae-sun the poet.</i>

1202
01:16:24,121 --> 01:16:27,124
<i>You learn about life</i>
<i>if you live through it.</i>

1203
01:16:28,917 --> 01:16:32,504
How shameful it would've been
if I gave up on life.

1204
01:16:33,255 --> 01:16:36,508
I'm so glad I lived all that I could.

1205
01:16:37,759 --> 01:16:41,680
So… your back in springtime now?

1206
01:16:42,848 --> 01:16:43,682
Mm-hmm.

1207
01:16:44,182 --> 01:16:45,601
It's spring again.

1208
01:16:46,435 --> 01:16:47,269
Um,

1209
01:16:48,770 --> 01:16:50,063
I thought life

1210
01:16:50,147 --> 01:16:53,609
went from spring to summer

1211
01:16:53,692 --> 01:16:55,694
to autumn to winter.

1212
01:16:56,987 --> 01:16:58,030
That's not

1213
01:16:59,906 --> 01:17:01,408
necessarily true.

1214
01:17:01,491 --> 01:17:03,035
Sometimes,

1215
01:17:04,119 --> 01:17:06,663
it's winter, sometimes it's spring.

1216
01:17:10,292 --> 01:17:12,711
I had lots of spring days, dear.

1217
01:17:12,794 --> 01:17:14,588
Many, many of those.

1218
01:17:17,299 --> 01:17:20,802
<i>The countless stars</i>
<i>of her years formed a galaxy.</i>

1219
01:17:21,762 --> 01:17:24,514
I've had many wonderful,

1220
01:17:25,932 --> 01:17:27,893
memorable moments.

1221
01:17:33,440 --> 01:17:36,026
There's seven years of my life
in the flower fields

1222
01:17:36,109 --> 01:17:37,778
living in this book.

1223
01:17:39,196 --> 01:17:42,157
<i>All the memories</i>
<i>that she kept close to her chest</i>

1224
01:17:42,240 --> 01:17:43,909
<i>were now in full bloom.</i>

1225
01:17:44,409 --> 01:17:45,577
So

1226
01:17:47,037 --> 01:17:47,913
are you happy?

1227
01:17:50,999 --> 01:17:51,833
Mm.

1228
01:17:53,043 --> 01:17:53,919
Oh yes.

1229
01:17:54,878 --> 01:17:56,630
I'm so

1230
01:17:56,713 --> 01:17:58,507
happy, yes.

1231
01:17:59,800 --> 01:18:03,762
<i>My mother's heart sparkled</i>
<i>in the most beautiful colors.</i>

1232
01:18:06,682 --> 01:18:08,517
<i>To my love,</i>

1233
01:18:09,851 --> 01:18:12,437
<i>from age nine to now,</i>

1234
01:18:13,438 --> 01:18:14,731
<i>my life</i>

1235
01:18:15,232 --> 01:18:18,276
<i>was always in spring because of you.</i>

1236
01:18:21,029 --> 01:18:23,240
<i>This book wouldn't exist</i>

1237
01:18:23,323 --> 01:18:24,991
<i>if it weren't for you.</i>

1238
01:18:26,743 --> 01:18:28,453
<i>I will live my life</i>

1239
01:18:29,496 --> 01:18:31,957
<i>as though every day is spring</i>

1240
01:18:32,040 --> 01:18:33,583
<i>until we meet again.</i>

1241
01:18:33,667 --> 01:18:34,501
Come here.

1242
01:18:38,130 --> 01:18:40,173
When I grow up to be a poet,

1243
01:18:40,257 --> 01:18:42,300
I'll wear two-piece outfits
like Um Aing-ran.

1244
01:18:42,968 --> 01:18:45,679
And, when I'm rich,
I'll live in a two-story house

1245
01:18:45,762 --> 01:18:47,889
and raise an adorable dog.

1246
01:18:47,973 --> 01:18:51,017
And I'll pay for
piano lessons for our kids.

1247
01:18:51,101 --> 01:18:53,019
I'll go out to eat nearly always.

1248
01:18:53,812 --> 01:18:58,024
Um, then I'll drive Jeeps
and wear Ray-Bans.

1249
01:18:58,525 --> 01:18:59,359
You love cars?

1250
01:19:00,318 --> 01:19:01,278
Yeah.

1251
01:19:01,361 --> 01:19:03,447
I didn't know you liked things.

1252
01:19:03,530 --> 01:19:06,992
I'm gonna take you
and drive that car all over the place.

1253
01:19:07,576 --> 01:19:08,994
I'm going to the States too.

1254
01:19:09,745 --> 01:19:11,371
Love it!

1255
01:19:12,581 --> 01:19:15,709
We can go together, chat,
do anything you want.

1256
01:19:15,792 --> 01:19:16,668
Love it.

1257
01:19:17,377 --> 01:19:18,295
I love it too.

1258
01:19:19,546 --> 01:19:22,591
Let's do all kinds of things
all our lives.

1259
01:19:22,674 --> 01:19:24,468
Let's do everything we'd like to.

1260
01:19:37,272 --> 01:19:39,816
<i>"To my parents</i>
<i>who were so young</i>

1261
01:19:39,900 --> 01:19:43,361
<i>and always so tender-hearted</i>
<i>all throughout the seasons."</i>

1262
01:19:43,862 --> 01:19:47,616
<i>"With remorse, gratitude,</i>
<i>and the deepest respect,</i>

1263
01:19:47,699 --> 01:19:49,868
<i>thanks for showing us what to do</i>

1264
01:19:51,077 --> 01:19:53,246
<i>when life gives you tangerines."</i>

1265
01:22:49,214 --> 01:22:54,219
"IF YOU CAN'T, JUST BACK DOWN.
WE'RE ALWAYS HERE FOR YOU."

